diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/README.md b/tests/kernel_dispatch/README.md
index dd7efb0..6c4eb49 100644
--- a/tests/kernel_dispatch/README.md
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/README.md
@@ -1,14 +1,190 @@
-# Kernel dispatch thread regression
+# Kernel dispatch regressions
 
 No game files are required. The test allocates synthetic guest memory and imports
 KeGetCurrentIrql and KeStallExecutionProcessor. It forces a lookup on another
 thread between the first lookup and its invocation. A shared dispatch slot
 selects the wrong service and pops an extra argument; per-thread storage passes.
 
+The handle test dispatches actual event and file imports across twelve workers
+and thirty-two synchronized cohorts. Registrations overlap removals of distinct
+objects; every live token and native handle stays unique, each event signals
+only its intended object, and each file returns its own payload. Native handle
+counts stay level and return after closure. Separate cases cover concurrent
+registration of one native handle, a single successful concurrent take, 64-bit
+handles, raw and pseudo handles, invalid tags, full-table ownership and reuse.
+Only registration and removal hold the table's writer lock; resolution uses a
+native atomic pointer load, and no native wait or I/O runs under that lock.
+
+The log tests dispatch 20,001 calls across three threads and wait beyond the
+summary interval. They verify that a zero budget stays quiet, a three-call
+budget emits exactly three unique trace lines, and `RECOMP_KERNEL_SUMMARY=1`
+retains accurate process-wide totals. Normal gameplay does not collect kernel
+summary counters or poll the summary clock after its boot trace budget ends.
+
+The sharing test opens an exclusive host file, verifies that the runtime
+returns `STATUS_SHARING_VIOLATION` consistently in the return value and I/O
+status block, and checks both native and guest-bridge DOS error conversion.
+The same open succeeds after the exclusive host handle closes. Two guest
+read-only opens with zero share access also succeed together for system link,
+while writers remain exclusive and real host sharing denials still propagate.
+It also interleaves a missing-file open on a streaming worker with the sharing
+conflict and a later successful open, verifying each thread's diagnostic error
+stays tied to its own call. A malformed guest name rejected before host I/O
+reports no Win32 error rather than inheriting the earlier sharing conflict.
+A zero-byte stream read retains `STATUS_END_OF_FILE`,
+zero bytes transferred and unchanged destination data.
+
+The critical-section test races lazy initialization across four threads,
+checks recursion and mutual exclusion for forty colliding table/cache keys,
+and verifies that bridge TryEnter and Leave use the same shadow as native
+Enter/Leave. Guest critical-section bytes remain unchanged. It also reports
+the cost of independent lock pairs without using timing as a pass condition.
+The default test also rejects disabled counter output; a second run with
+`RECOMP_CS_COUNTERS=1` verifies the optional contention totals are reported.
+`RECOMP_CS_TRACE_CRT` and `RECOMP_CS_WATCH` also enable those accurate counters.
+
+The GPU notification wait test uses the runtime's exact host helper without
+starting a renderer. It checks completion before waiting, a completion injected
+between the predicate check and native wait, GET/NOP/shutdown wakeups, spurious
+wakes, concurrent guest waiters, unavailable-API fallback, and guest register
+changes without an executor notification. Host waits are bounded to 1 ms;
+only the original guest completion conditions can end the wait.
+
+The direct fence test preserves the title's unsigned subtraction/comparison,
+including wrap boundaries and a completed value ahead of the submitted value.
+It also checks completion before waiting, a publication in the check-to-wait
+interval, wakeups without completion, shutdown, and timeout/API fallback. The
+host helper never modifies the guest fence value.
+
+The contiguous-range cache test uses real allocations, frees, splits and
+coalescing. Positive thread-local hints retain only bounds proven covered by
+the allocation table; misses always check the locked table. Cases include
+adjacent allocations, holes, physical aliases, range overflow, cache collisions,
+and allocations made by another thread after an earlier miss. Freeing a block
+does not erase its permanent physical ownership or invalidate that coverage.
+
+The command-fence test dispatches actual NV097 semaphore methods through the
+executor. `xbox_Nv2aCommandFence` configures an existing fence mirror before
+guest entry: only the matching DMA context, semaphore offset and executed
+release value can complete it. The next guest counter cannot complete work
+during startup or an idle tick. Releases retain their targets at execution,
+preserve ordering across target changes and unsigned wrap, and wait for prior
+readbacks and a fully consumed GET checkpoint. Incomplete parser passes retain
+their releases. Other titles keep the generic counter-snapshot mirror behavior.
+The native-heap allocation fallback is tested without an early fence, GET,
+notification or GPU-readback publication.
+
+The DMA synchronization test exercises the real publication and completion
+functions. `xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish` writes the owned PFIFO PUT and PGRAPH busy state
+before exposing USER PUT. The first publication adopts the actual USER GET;
+later completions advance USER/PFIFO GET to their captured consumed boundary.
+A brief shared lock prevents an older completion from clearing a newer PUT's
+busy state. Publishing an already completed PUT stays idle, while a software
+channel keeps its original store. `xbox_Nv2aDmaWait` waits only for the original
+CACHE1 PUT/GET equality and zero PGRAPH status, with the original final guest
+reads retained. Tests cover concurrent stores, older completions, raw register
+updates, unknown apertures, shutdown and completion before native registration.
+
+Matching NOPs are recorded during execution without waking the guest. Their
+exact notification sequence is published after the corresponding consumed GET
+and prior readbacks. A held older GET retains its own sequence, so its release
+cannot expose a NOP from a newer incomplete pass. Tests assert both GET stores
+at notification wake time, a newer live PUT, incomplete-pass deferral and
+notification-count wrap. Native notification, fence and DMA waits snapshot the
+wake generation before rechecking their predicates; a wake alone never changes
+the guest completion rules.
+
+The pushbuffer hitch test feeds increasing/non-increasing packets, a CALL and
+RETURN, and a jump through the real decoder with tracing both off and on.
+Deterministic clocks verify a slow draw is identified separately from normal
+flip pacing, while quiet mode reads no diagnostic clocks. Commands and their
+parameters arrive unchanged and in their original order.
+It also splits increasing and non-increasing payloads across multiple PUT
+updates, including values that resemble CALL/JUMP/RETURN headers. Further
+cases cover real ring jumps, called lists and root payloads crossing the
+64 MiB physical boundary, discontinuous scans, and empty packets.
+Called lists stop at the actual PUT even before a header or within its payload,
+and later publication resumes the saved return address. Reserved header bits,
+exact RETURN decoding and method-address wrapping follow
+[xemu's PFIFO implementation](https://github.com/xemu-project/xemu/blob/master/hw/xbox/nv2a/pfifo.c).
+Work-limit tests stop in root and called payloads, report incomplete consumption,
+and resume once without duplicating commands, including a larger PUT on retry.
+
+The `nv2a-pb-capture` case checks the opt-in `RECOMP_PB_CAPTURE=<path-prefix>`
+diagnostic. On the first parser work-limit hit it writes these version-1
+artifacts, then stops recording:
+
+| Suffix | Contents |
+| --- | --- |
+| `.json` | Parser start/end, saved packet/CALL state, record sizes/counts, ring bounds and individual write-success flags. |
+| `.reads.bin` | First 1,048,576 words fetched in that pass, before executor callbacks; each 24-byte record contains six little-endian `uint32_t` fields: `va`, `word`, `method`, `remaining`, `flags`, `return_va`. Flag 1 marks a payload and flag 2 marks an active CALL. |
+| `.recent.bin` | Last 256 fetched records in chronological order, using the same schema. |
+| `.ram.bin` | The 64 MiB contiguous RAM window at the limit hit; guest address `0x80000000` is byte zero. |
+| `.initial-ring.bin` | Configured producer ring copied before the pass, including its boundary JUMP word; `initial_ring_va` and `initial_ring_bytes` locate it. The copy is limited to 4 MiB. |
+| `.state-initial.bin`, `.state-final.bin` | `XBOX_NV2A_CAPTURE_STATE` snapshots before execution and at the limit. |
+| `.producer.json` | Named initial/final USER/PFIFO pointers, held GET, notification state and registered fence/device fields. |
+
+The state snapshots are zero-initialized, read-only diagnostic structures from
+`xbox_memory_layout.h`. Version 1 is 35,272 bytes: an 18-word header followed by
+four mirrors, each with 24 metadata words and a `0x2200`-byte raw device block.
+The header carries the version and total byte size. Validity flags and
+`device_bytes` distinguish unavailable data from a real zero. Registered device
+pointers supply the roots; the helper does not hardcode the MM3 image global.
+The snapshots and ring copies do not suspend the producer and are not atomic;
+the fetched-word ledger is the evidence of what execution actually read.
+
+Capture mode allocates and copies extra memory and can write roughly 89 MiB
+at its first limit, so use it for an isolated diagnosis rather than performance
+measurements. With capture disabled there are no capture allocations, extra RAM
+copies, snapshot calls or file writes. The regression verifies pre-callback
+word preservation, lengths/schema and unchanged host LastError, then removes
+only its own artifacts.
+
+Timer lifecycle cases cover signal publication before callbacks, rearming,
+retired timer storage, periodic cancellation, and absolute/relative deadlines.
+The `audio_deadline` case mirrors MM3's future-deadline rearm loop: one action
+must require one callback, rather than running again on every polling tick.
+DPC cancellation cases exercise wrapped FIFO order, duplicate rejection, and
+1,000 insert/cancel cycles without losing queue capacity.
+
+The lower-IRQL cases require pending completions to run before the lowering
+thread resumes object destruction. They check register, x87, MMX, XMM and host
+floating-point state preservation, nested callbacks, the DISPATCH boundary,
+and DPC-active state. Callback frames use an independent guest stack; a USB
+request-shaped sentinel below the interrupted stack pointer must survive.
+Stack-pool exhaustion is also exercised. Thread-layout cases verify that the
+full KPCR, including `FS+0x58`, cannot alias the title's TLS and that a new
+thread starts with clear IRQL and DPC state.
+
+Async-wait trace cases compare real success, zero-timeout and invalid-handle
+outcomes through the dispatcher with native HLE outcomes. They verify register,
+x87, stack and host LastError preservation; guarded reads from uncommitted
+memory; separate ordinary/failure budgets per wait kind; explicit
+trace-disable precedence; and unchanged default behavior for title-built
+KEVENTs. The inline case explicitly enables that existing option for the test.
+
+The inline-event caller cases exercise the public startup-only
+`xbox_kernel_set_inline_event_callers` API with MM3's verified XPP setter and
+wait return PCs. The global `RECOMP_TITLE_KEVENTS` option stays disabled.
+Real native completion workers pass through the kernel dispatch bridge,
+including completion before the first wait and completion while it blocks.
+A request-shaped sentinel must remain intact until completion. The timeout
+case follows XPP's 50 ms timeout and subsequent cancellation wait; a negative
+control reproduces the old invalid-handle return and released request storage.
+
+Further cases check notification versus synchronization signal consumption,
+unrelated callers at an already shadowed address, ordinary initialized events,
+invalid headers and uncommitted/read-only pointers, repeated stack reuse with
+event-type changes, full shadow-table behavior, host handle counts, and
+concurrent first registration. No title assets or game process are required.
+
 On Windows with Visual Studio:
 
 ```
 cmake -S tests/kernel_dispatch -B build/kernel-dispatch -A x64
-cmake --build build/kernel-dispatch --config Release --target kernel-dispatch-thread-test
+cmake --build build/kernel-dispatch --config Release
 ctest --test-dir build/kernel-dispatch -C Release --output-on-failure
 ```
+
+Build all targets before running CTest so the timer, DPC and thread-layout
+regressions are included.
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/contig_heap_ownership_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/contig_heap_ownership_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8acb74b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/contig_heap_ownership_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,152 @@
+/* Exercise production heap/contiguous ownership with a private host arena.
+ * Heap high-water marks include addresses skipped over contiguous blocks;
+ * only blocks actually issued by the heap reserve physical addresses. */
+#include "kernel.h"
+#include "xbox_memory_layout.h"
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+#include "../../src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.c"
+
+void *recomp_lookup(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+void *recomp_lookup_manual(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+
+#define CHECK(expr) do { if (!(expr)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #expr); exit(1); \
+} } while (0)
+
+static uint8_t *guest_bytes(uint32_t address)
+{
+    return (uint8_t *)((uintptr_t)address + g_memory_offset);
+}
+
+static void expect_bytes(uint32_t address, uint32_t size, uint8_t value)
+{
+    const uint8_t *bytes = guest_bytes(address);
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < size; ++i) CHECK(bytes[i] == value);
+}
+
+static void check_ownership(void)
+{
+    /* Freed blocks still own their physical addresses in both tables. */
+    for (LONG i = 0; i < g_contig_alloc_count; ++i) {
+        uint32_t begin = g_contig_allocs[i].offset;
+        uint64_t end = (uint64_t)begin + g_contig_allocs[i].size;
+        CHECK(begin >= 0x1000u && !(begin & 0xFFFu));
+        CHECK(!(g_contig_allocs[i].size & 0xFFFu));
+        CHECK(end <= XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE - XBOX_GPU_INSTANCE_DEFAULT);
+        if (i) CHECK((uint64_t)g_contig_allocs[i - 1].offset +
+                     g_contig_allocs[i - 1].size <= begin);
+        CHECK(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(begin, g_contig_allocs[i].size));
+        for (int j = 0; j < g_heap_block_count; ++j) {
+            uint64_t heap_end = (uint64_t)g_heap_blocks[j].addr + g_heap_blocks[j].size;
+            CHECK(end <= g_heap_blocks[j].addr || heap_end <= begin);
+        }
+    }
+    for (int i = 0; i < g_heap_block_count; ++i)
+        CHECK(!xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(g_heap_blocks[i].addr, 1));
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+    const size_t reservation = (size_t)XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE;
+    uint8_t *arena = VirtualAlloc(NULL, reservation, MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    uint32_t heap, heap_cross, heap_later, first, aligned, fill, after_heap, reused, gap;
+    uint32_t alignment_gap, second_alignment_gap, large_alignment_gap, heap_skip_gap;
+    CHECK(arena);
+    CHECK(VirtualAlloc(arena + XBOX_CONTIG_BASE, XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE,
+                       MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE));
+    CHECK(VirtualAlloc(arena + XBOX_HEAP_BASE, 0x20000,
+                       MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE));
+    g_memory_offset = (ptrdiff_t)arena;
+    InitializeCriticalSection(&g_allocator_lock);
+    g_allocator_lock_initialized = 1;
+    SetEnvironmentVariableA("RECOMP_CONTIG_TRACE", NULL);
+
+    heap = xbox_HeapAlloc(0x2000, 4096);
+    CHECK(heap == XBOX_HEAP_BASE);
+    memset(guest_bytes(heap), 0xA5, 0x2000);
+    first = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 4096);
+    aligned = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 0x10000);
+    CHECK(first == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x1000);
+    CHECK(aligned == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x10000);
+    CHECK(!xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(0x2000, 1));
+    fill = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(XBOX_HEAP_BASE - 0x11000, 4096);
+    CHECK(fill == aligned + 0x1000);
+    after_heap = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x4000, 4096);
+    CHECK(after_heap == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + heap + 0x2000);
+    check_ownership();
+    expect_bytes(heap, 0x2000, 0xA5);
+
+    /* Ordinary heap growth skips an existing contiguous block. Alignment
+     * then leaves another unissued gap below its high-water mark. */
+    heap_cross = xbox_HeapAlloc(0x3000, 4096);
+    CHECK(heap_cross == heap + 0x6000);
+    CHECK(g_heap_next > after_heap - XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x4000);
+    memset(guest_bytes(heap_cross), 0x3C, 0x3000);
+    heap_later = xbox_HeapAlloc(0x3000, 0x10000);
+    CHECK(heap_later == heap + 0x10000);
+    memset(guest_bytes(heap_later), 0x5A, 0x3000);
+    memset(guest_bytes(after_heap), 0xC3, 0x4000);
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(after_heap - XBOX_CONTIG_BASE, 0x4000));
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousFree(after_heap));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ContiguousBlockSize(after_heap));
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(after_heap - XBOX_CONTIG_BASE, 0x4000));
+    reused = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x4000, 4096);
+    CHECK(reused == after_heap);
+    expect_bytes(reused, 0x4000, 0);
+    gap = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x3000, 4096);
+    CHECK(gap == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + heap + 0x9000);
+    CHECK(!xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(heap + 0xC000, 1));
+    check_ownership();
+    expect_bytes(heap, 0x2000, 0xA5);
+    expect_bytes(heap_cross, 0x3000, 0x3C);
+    expect_bytes(heap_later, 0x3000, 0x5A);
+
+    xbox_HeapFree(heap);
+    CHECK(!xbox_HeapBlockSize(heap));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(heap, 0x2000));
+    expect_bytes(heap, 0x2000, 0xA5);
+
+    /* Simulate an exhausted bump without issuing every remaining page. Only
+     * the bump changes: production tables still describe the real holes.
+     * The fallback must insert these new lower offsets in sorted order. */
+    g_contig_next = XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE - XBOX_GPU_INSTANCE_DEFAULT;
+    alignment_gap = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 0x4000);
+    CHECK(alignment_gap == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x4000);
+    CHECK(!(alignment_gap & 0x3FFF));
+    second_alignment_gap = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x2000, 0x4000);
+    CHECK(second_alignment_gap == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x8000);
+    CHECK(!(second_alignment_gap & 0x3FFF));
+    large_alignment_gap = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x6000, 4096);
+    CHECK(large_alignment_gap == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xA000);
+    heap_skip_gap = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x4000, 4096);
+    CHECK(heap_skip_gap == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + heap + 0xC000);
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(heap + 0x2000, 0x4000));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(heap + 0x6000, 1));
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(heap + 0x9000, 0x7000));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(heap + 0x10000, 1));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(0x3000, 2));
+    check_ownership();
+    expect_bytes(heap, 0x2000, 0xA5);
+    expect_bytes(heap_cross, 0x3000, 0x3C);
+    expect_bytes(heap_later, 0x3000, 0x5A);
+
+    /* Heap free/reuse cannot transfer its address to contiguous storage. */
+    CHECK(xbox_HeapAlloc(0x2000, 4096) == heap);
+    expect_bytes(heap, 0x2000, 0);
+    expect_bytes(heap_cross, 0x3000, 0x3C);
+    expect_bytes(heap_later, 0x3000, 0x5A);
+    check_ownership();
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousFree(alignment_gap));
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(0x4000, 0x1000));
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 0x4000) == alignment_gap);
+    check_ownership();
+
+    puts("contiguous exact heap ownership and exhausted-arena gap reuse passed");
+    DeleteCriticalSection(&g_allocator_lock);
+    CHECK(VirtualFree(arena, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/contig_range_cache_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/contig_range_cache_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..88b6e78
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/contig_range_cache_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,209 @@
+/* Exercise the production allocator and its positive DMA coverage hints.
+ * A private arena replaces only memory-layout initialization, not allocation. */
+#include "kernel.h"
+#include "xbox_memory_layout.h"
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+static RECOMP_TLS unsigned lock_entries;
+static void counted_enter(CRITICAL_SECTION *lock)
+{
+    ++lock_entries;
+    EnterCriticalSection(lock);
+}
+#define EnterCriticalSection counted_enter
+#include "../../src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.c"
+#undef EnterCriticalSection
+
+void *recomp_lookup(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+void *recomp_lookup_manual(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+
+#define CHECK(expr) do { if (!(expr)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #expr); exit(1); \
+} } while (0)
+
+static int uncached_range(uint32_t offset, uint32_t size)
+{
+    uint64_t end = (uint64_t)offset + (size ? size : 1u);
+    uint32_t begin, covered;
+    if (offset >= XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE || end > XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE)
+        return 0;
+    return contig_range_lookup(offset, end, &begin, &covered);
+}
+
+static void expect_range(uint32_t offset, uint32_t size, int result)
+{
+    CHECK(uncached_range(offset, size) == result);
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(offset, size) == result);
+}
+
+typedef struct {
+    HANDLE ready, proceed;
+    uint32_t positive, future;
+    unsigned first_locks, repeat_locks, miss_locks, new_locks;
+    int positive_before, positive_after, missed, found;
+} WORKER;
+
+static DWORD WINAPI check_worker(LPVOID argument)
+{
+    WORKER *w = argument;
+    lock_entries = 0;
+    w->positive_before = xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(w->positive, 0x3000);
+    w->first_locks = lock_entries;
+    lock_entries = 0;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 1000; ++i)
+        if (!xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(w->positive + (i & 0xFFF), 1))
+            w->positive_before = 0;
+    w->repeat_locks = lock_entries;
+    lock_entries = 0;
+    w->missed = !xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(w->future, 1) &&
+                !xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(w->future, 1);
+    w->miss_locks = lock_entries;
+    SetEvent(w->ready);
+    WaitForSingleObject(w->proceed, INFINITE);
+    lock_entries = 0;
+    w->positive_after = xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(w->positive, 0x3000);
+    CHECK(lock_entries == 0);
+    w->found = xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(w->future, 0x1000);
+    w->new_locks = lock_entries;
+    lock_entries = 0;
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(w->future + 0xFFF, 0));
+    CHECK(lock_entries == 0);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static double bench(int (*volatile query)(uint32_t, uint32_t), uint32_t offset)
+{
+    LARGE_INTEGER start, end, frequency;
+    volatile unsigned total = 0;
+    QueryPerformanceFrequency(&frequency);
+    QueryPerformanceCounter(&start);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 200000; ++i)
+        total += query(offset + (i & 0xFFF), (i & 63) + 1);
+    QueryPerformanceCounter(&end);
+    CHECK(total == 200000);
+    return 1e9 * (double)(end.QuadPart - start.QuadPart) /
+           (double)frequency.QuadPart / 200000;
+}
+
+static int compare_double(const void *a, const void *b)
+{
+    double x = *(const double *)a, y = *(const double *)b;
+    return (x > y) - (x < y);
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+    const size_t reservation = (size_t)XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE;
+    uint8_t *arena = VirtualAlloc(NULL, reservation, MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    uint32_t a, b, c, heap, fill, after_heap, split, fresh;
+    uint32_t isolated[40];
+    WORKER worker = {0};
+    HANDLE thread;
+    double cached[7], locked[7];
+    CHECK(arena);
+    CHECK(VirtualAlloc(arena + XBOX_CONTIG_BASE, XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE,
+                       MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE));
+    CHECK(VirtualAlloc(arena + XBOX_HEAP_BASE, 0x10000,
+                       MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE));
+    g_memory_offset = (ptrdiff_t)arena;
+    InitializeCriticalSection(&g_allocator_lock);
+    g_allocator_lock_initialized = 1;
+    SetEnvironmentVariableA("RECOMP_CONTIG_TRACE", NULL);
+
+    expect_range(0x1000, 1, 0);
+    expect_range(0, 0, 0);
+    heap = xbox_HeapAlloc(0x2000, 4096);
+    CHECK(heap == XBOX_HEAP_BASE);
+    a = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(1, 4096);
+    b = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x2000, 4096);
+    c = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 0x10000);
+    CHECK(a == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x1000);
+    CHECK(b == a + 0x1000);
+    CHECK(c == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x10000);
+    expect_range(0x1000, 0x3000, 1); /* Adjacent allocations are continuous. */
+    expect_range(0x1FFF, 0, 1);      /* Zero means one byte, including page tail. */
+    expect_range(0x3FFF, 1, 1);
+    expect_range(0x3FFF, 2, 0);
+    expect_range(0x4000, 1, 0);      /* Alignment holes do not become coverage. */
+    expect_range(0x10000, 0x1000, 1);
+    expect_range(0xFFF0, 32, 0);
+
+    /* Real heap ownership forces the next contiguous allocation to skip it. */
+    fill = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(XBOX_HEAP_BASE - (g_contig_next - XBOX_CONTIG_BASE), 4096);
+    CHECK(fill == c + 0x1000);
+    after_heap = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 4096);
+    CHECK(after_heap == XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + heap + 0x2000);
+    expect_range(heap - 1, 1, 1);
+    expect_range(heap, 1, 0);
+    expect_range(heap - 1, 2, 0);
+    expect_range(heap, 0x2001, 0);
+    expect_range(after_heap - XBOX_CONTIG_BASE, 0x1000, 1);
+    xbox_HeapFree(heap);
+    CHECK(xbox_HeapBlockSize(heap) == 0);
+    expect_range(heap, 0x2000, 0); /* Ordinary heap free does not change ownership. */
+
+    /* A cached union remains covered after entries coalesce and split. */
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousFree(a));
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousFree(b | 0x20000000u));
+    expect_range(0x1000, 0x3000, 1);
+    split = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 0x2000);
+    CHECK(split == b);
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousBlockSize(split) == 0x1000);
+    expect_range(0x1000, 0x3000, 1);
+    expect_range(0x3000, 0x1000, 1); /* Freed tail still backs DMA. */
+
+    /* Eviction and hash collisions must never fill the intervening gaps. */
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 40; ++i) {
+        isolated[i] = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 0x10000) - XBOX_CONTIG_BASE;
+        CHECK(isolated[i] && (isolated[i] & 0xFFFF) == 0);
+    }
+    for (unsigned round = 0; round < 3; ++round)
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 40; ++i) {
+            expect_range(isolated[i], 0x1000, 1);
+            expect_range(isolated[i] + 0x1000, 1, 0);
+        }
+    expect_range(a, 1, 0); /* This API accepts physical offsets, not aliases. */
+    expect_range(a | 0x20000000u, 1, 0);
+    expect_range(UINT32_MAX - 0x1000, 0x2000, 0);
+    expect_range(0x1000, UINT32_MAX, 0);
+    expect_range(XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE - 1, 2, 0);
+    expect_range(XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE, 0, 0);
+
+    worker.positive = 0x1000;
+    worker.future = ((g_contig_next + 0xFFFF) & ~0xFFFFu) - XBOX_CONTIG_BASE;
+    worker.ready = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    worker.proceed = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    CHECK(worker.ready && worker.proceed);
+    thread = CreateThread(NULL, 0, check_worker, &worker, 0, NULL);
+    CHECK(thread && WaitForSingleObject(worker.ready, 5000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    CHECK(worker.positive_before && worker.first_locks == 1);
+    CHECK(worker.repeat_locks == 0 && worker.missed && worker.miss_locks == 2);
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousFree(split));
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 0x2000) == split);
+    fresh = xbox_ContiguousAlloc(0x1000, 0x10000);
+    CHECK(fresh - XBOX_CONTIG_BASE == worker.future);
+    SetEvent(worker.proceed);
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(thread, 5000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    CHECK(worker.positive_after && worker.found && worker.new_locks == 1);
+    CloseHandle(thread);
+    CloseHandle(worker.ready);
+    CloseHandle(worker.proceed);
+
+    /* Informational medians exercise the actual exported query against the
+     * same exact locked lookup. No timing threshold is a regression gate. */
+    CHECK(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated(0x1000, 0x3000));
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 7; ++i) {
+        cached[i] = bench(xbox_ContiguousRangeAllocated, 0x1000);
+        locked[i] = bench(uncached_range, 0x1000);
+    }
+    qsort(cached, 7, sizeof cached[0], compare_double);
+    qsort(locked, 7, sizeof locked[0], compare_double);
+    printf("contiguous coverage cache passed; median cached=%.2f ns locked=%.2f ns\n",
+           cached[3], locked[3]);
+    DeleteCriticalSection(&g_allocator_lock);
+    CHECK(VirtualFree(arena, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_async_wait_trace_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_async_wait_trace_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..13fac04
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_async_wait_trace_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@
+/* Exercise real wait bridges and HLE without game assets. */
+#include "../../src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c"
+#include <io.h>
+
+#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { printf("FAIL line %d: %s status=%08X host_error=%lu\n", __LINE__, #c, g_eax, GetLastError()); fflush(stdout); exit(1); } } while (0)
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup(uint32_t address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup_manual(uint32_t address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static unsigned occurrences(const char *text, const char *needle) {
+    unsigned n = 0;
+    while ((text = strstr(text, needle)) != NULL) { ++n; text += strlen(needle); }
+    return n;
+}
+
+static void invoke(unsigned ordinal, uint32_t object, uint32_t expected, DWORD expected_error) {
+    uint32_t *stack = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x20000);
+    uint8_t before[0x200];
+    g_esp = 0x20000; g_eax = 0xBAD;
+    g_ecx = 0x11223344; g_edx = 0x22334455; g_ebx = 0x33445566;
+    g_esi = 0x30000; g_edi = 0x44556677; g_ebp = 0x55667788;
+    g_seh_ebp = 0x66778899; g_df = 1; g_fp_top = 3; g_fp_cmp = -1;
+    g_fp_control_word = 0x37F; g_fp_cc = 0x4100;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 8; ++i) g_fp_stack[i] = i * 1.25 - 3.0;
+    memset(stack, 0, 0x200);
+    stack[0] = 0x0035C7F1; stack[1] = object;
+    stack[ordinal == 159 ? 5 : ordinal == 233 ? 3 : 4] = 0x28000;
+    memcpy(before, stack, sizeof before);
+    SetLastError(0x1234);
+    recomp_func_t fn = recomp_lookup_kernel(KERNEL_VA_BASE + (ordinal == 159 ? 0 : ordinal == 233 ? 4 : 8));
+    CHECK(fn != NULL);
+    fn();
+    if (g_eax != expected || GetLastError() != expected_error) {
+        printf("wait ordinal=%u object=%08X expected=%08X error=%lu actual=%08X error=%lu\n",
+               ordinal, object, expected, expected_error, g_eax, GetLastError());
+        fflush(stdout);
+    }
+    CHECK(g_eax == expected && GetLastError() == expected_error);
+    CHECK(g_esp == 0x20004 + (ordinal == 159 ? 20 : ordinal == 233 ? 12 : 16));
+    CHECK(g_xbox_kernel_caller == 0x0035C7F1);
+    CHECK(g_ecx == 0x11223344 && g_edx == 0x22334455);
+    CHECK(g_ebx == 0x33445566 && g_esi == 0x30000 && g_edi == 0x44556677);
+    CHECK(g_ebp == 0x55667788 && g_seh_ebp == 0x66778899 && g_df == 1);
+    CHECK(g_fp_top == 3 && g_fp_cmp == -1 && g_fp_control_word == 0x37F && g_fp_cc == 0x4100);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 8; ++i) CHECK(g_fp_stack[i] == i * 1.25 - 3.0);
+    CHECK(memcmp(before, stack, sizeof before) == 0);
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char **argv) {
+    int inline_events = argc > 1 && strcmp(argv[1], "inline") == 0;
+    int tracing = argc > 1 && strcmp(argv[1], "off") != 0;
+    int override = argc > 1 && strcmp(argv[1], "override") == 0;
+    FILE *captured;
+    int saved;
+    char *output = malloc(400000);
+    HANDLE signaled, unsignaled;
+    uint32_t on_token, off_token;
+    DWORD native_error;
+    NTSTATUS native_status;
+    LARGE_INTEGER zero = {0};
+    CHECK(output != NULL);
+    CHECK(_putenv_s("RECOMP_ASYNC_WAIT_TRACE", tracing && !override ? "1" : "0") == 0);
+    CHECK(_putenv_s("MM3_BUILDING_TRACE", override ? "1" : "0") == 0);
+    CHECK(_putenv_s("RECOMP_TITLE_KEVENTS", inline_events ? "1" : "0") == 0);
+    CHECK(_putenv_s("RECOMP_KERNEL_LOG_BUDGET", "0") == 0);
+    CHECK(_putenv_s("RECOMP_GUEST_LOCK", "0") == 0);
+    if (override) tracing = 0;
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 0x100000, MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_NOACCESS);
+    CHECK(memory && VirtualAlloc(memory, 0x40000, MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE) == memory);
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory;
+    g_xbox_map_size = 0x100000;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
+        unsigned ordinal = i == 0 ? 159 : i == 1 ? 233 : 234;
+        g_slot_ordinals[i] = ordinal;
+        g_slot_bridges[i] = bridge_for_ordinal(ordinal);
+        g_slot_arg_bytes[i] = stdcall_args_for_ordinal(ordinal);
+    }
+    signaled = CreateEventA(NULL, TRUE, TRUE, NULL);
+    unsignaled = CreateEventA(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    CHECK(signaled && unsignaled);
+    on_token = bridge_handle_token(signaled); off_token = bridge_handle_token(unsignaled);
+    CHECK(on_token && off_token);
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x30000) = 0x1020;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x30004) = 0x103;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x30008) = 0x0035C33A;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x3000C) = 0x22000;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x22000) = 0x00040000; /* title-built notification KEVENT */
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x22004) = 1;
+    fflush(stderr); captured = tmpfile(); saved = _dup(_fileno(stderr));
+    CHECK(captured && saved >= 0 && _dup2(_fileno(captured), _fileno(stderr)) == 0);
+    /* These diagnostic pointers are reserved but have no committed backing. */
+    g_esp = 0x50000; g_eax = 0; SetLastError(0x9988);
+    g_xbox_kernel_caller = 0;
+    bridge_async_wait_log(159, 0x50000, NULL, "probe", 0, 0);
+    CHECK(GetLastError() == 0x9988 && g_esp == 0x50000 && g_eax == 0);
+    {
+        int type;
+        HANDLE guest_event = ke_guest_event(0x22000, &type);
+        CHECK((guest_event != NULL) == inline_events);
+        SetLastError(0x1234);
+        native_status = xbox_KeWaitForSingleObject(inline_events ? guest_event : (HANDLE)(uintptr_t)0x22000,
+                                                  0, 0, 0, &zero);
+        native_error = GetLastError();
+        invoke(159, 0x22000, (uint32_t)native_status, native_error);
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(0x22004) == 1);
+    }
+    for (unsigned kind = 0; kind < 3; ++kind) {
+        unsigned ordinal = kind == 0 ? 159 : kind == 1 ? 233 : 234;
+        SetLastError(0x1234);
+        native_status = xbox_KeWaitForSingleObject(signaled, 0, 0, 0, &zero); native_error = GetLastError();
+        CHECK(native_status == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+        invoke(ordinal, on_token, (uint32_t)native_status, native_error);
+        SetLastError(0x1234);
+        native_status = xbox_KeWaitForSingleObject(unsignaled, 0, 0, 0, &zero); native_error = GetLastError();
+        CHECK(native_status == STATUS_TIMEOUT);
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 40; ++i) invoke(ordinal, off_token, (uint32_t)native_status, native_error);
+        SetLastError(0x1234);
+        native_status = xbox_KeWaitForSingleObject((HANDLE)(uintptr_t)0x50000000, 0, 0, 0, &zero);
+        native_error = GetLastError();
+        CHECK(native_status & 0x80000000u);
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 70; ++i) invoke(ordinal, 0x50000000, (uint32_t)native_status, native_error);
+    }
+    fflush(stderr); CHECK(_dup2(saved, _fileno(stderr)) == 0); _close(saved);
+    rewind(captured);
+    size_t length = fread(output, 1, 399999, captured); output[length] = 0; fclose(captured);
+    /* Polling uses its own budget; later failures still produce 64 records. */
+    CHECK(occurrences(output, "[ASYNC_WAIT]") == (tracing ? 3 * (32 + 64) : 0));
+    if (tracing) {
+        CHECK(strstr(output, "caller=0035C7F1"));
+        CHECK(strstr(output, "request_callback=0035C33A request_context=00022000"));
+        CHECK(strstr(output, "status=00000102"));
+        CHECK(strstr(output, "requested=00050000") && strstr(output, "header_read=0"));
+        CHECK(strstr(output, "request_read=1 request_status=00000103"));
+        CHECK(strstr(output, "stack_read=0"));
+        if (inline_events) CHECK(strstr(output, "kind=inline_kevent"));
+    }
+    CloseHandle(signaled); CloseHandle(unsignaled);
+    VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE); free(output);
+    printf("PASS: async wait trace %s preserves real wait status, registers, memory and host error; separate bounded polling/failure budgets\n", argv[1]);
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_cs_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_cs_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..010fbf0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_cs_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,183 @@
+/* Permanent shadow caches must preserve native exclusion and recursion. */
+#include "kernel.h"
+#include "xbox_memory_layout.h"
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+typedef void (*guest_fn)(void);
+extern guest_fn recomp_lookup_kernel(uint32_t);
+extern RECOMP_TLS uint32_t g_eax, g_esp;
+extern ptrdiff_t g_xbox_mem_offset;
+void *recomp_lookup(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+void *recomp_lookup_manual(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+
+#define THREADS 4
+#define COLLISIONS 40
+#define SHARED_ITERATIONS 5000
+#define COLLISION_ITERATIONS 100
+#define BENCH_ITERATIONS 100000
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static HANDLE start_event;
+static volatile LONG failed, active;
+static uint32_t shared_count, collision_count[COLLISIONS];
+static uint32_t imports[2];
+
+static PRTL_CRITICAL_SECTION guest_lock(unsigned i)
+{
+    /* Every address shares the table bucket and thread-cache bucket. */
+    return (PRTL_CRITICAL_SECTION)(memory + 0x10000 + i * 0x10000);
+}
+
+typedef struct { unsigned id, phase; } WORKER;
+static DWORD WINAPI worker(LPVOID p)
+{
+    WORKER *w = p;
+    WaitForSingleObject(start_event, INFINITE);
+    if (w->phase == 0) {
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < SHARED_ITERATIONS; i++) {
+            PRTL_CRITICAL_SECTION lock = guest_lock(0);
+            /* The first call races lazy initialization across all workers. */
+            xbox_RtlEnterCriticalSection(lock);
+            xbox_RtlEnterCriticalSection(lock);
+            if (active) InterlockedExchange(&failed, 1);
+            active = 1;
+            shared_count++;
+            if ((i & 255) == 0) SwitchToThread();
+            active = 0;
+            xbox_RtlLeaveCriticalSection(lock);
+            xbox_RtlLeaveCriticalSection(lock);
+        }
+    } else if (w->phase == 1) {
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < COLLISION_ITERATIONS; i++)
+            for (unsigned j = 0; j < COLLISIONS; j++) {
+                PRTL_CRITICAL_SECTION lock = guest_lock(j);
+                xbox_RtlEnterCriticalSection(lock);
+                collision_count[j]++;
+                xbox_RtlLeaveCriticalSection(lock);
+            }
+    } else {
+        /* Independent repeated locks expose table contention without a
+         * guest-lock bottleneck. Timing is informational, never a pass gate. */
+        PRTL_CRITICAL_SECTION lock = guest_lock(w->id);
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < BENCH_ITERATIONS; i++) {
+            xbox_RtlEnterCriticalSection(lock);
+            xbox_RtlLeaveCriticalSection(lock);
+        }
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static int run_workers(unsigned phase)
+{
+    HANDLE threads[THREADS];
+    WORKER workers[THREADS];
+    ResetEvent(start_event);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < THREADS; i++) {
+        workers[i].id = i;
+        workers[i].phase = phase;
+        threads[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, worker, &workers[i], 0, NULL);
+        if (!threads[i]) abort();
+    }
+    SetEvent(start_event);
+    DWORD wait = WaitForMultipleObjects(THREADS, threads, TRUE, 30000);
+    if (wait != WAIT_OBJECT_0) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: lock phase %u timed out\n", phase);
+        /* Worker parameters are on this stack; do not return with live users. */
+        ExitProcess(2);
+    }
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < THREADS; i++) CloseHandle(threads[i]);
+    return !failed;
+}
+
+static uint32_t invoke(unsigned slot)
+{
+    guest_fn fn = recomp_lookup_kernel(imports[slot]);
+    uint32_t *sp;
+    if (!fn) abort();
+    g_esp = 0x700000;
+    sp = (uint32_t *)(memory + g_esp);
+    sp[0] = 0xBEEF0001;
+    sp[1] = 0x10000;
+    fn();
+    if (g_esp != 0x700008) InterlockedExchange(&failed, 1);
+    return g_eax;
+}
+
+static DWORD WINAPI probe_try(LPVOID p)
+{
+    int expected = *(int *)p;
+    uint32_t got = invoke(0);
+    if (got != (uint32_t)expected) InterlockedExchange(&failed, 1);
+    if (got) invoke(1);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static int try_from_other_thread(int expected)
+{
+    HANDLE thread = CreateThread(NULL, 0, probe_try, &expected, 0, NULL);
+    if (!thread) return 0;
+    if (WaitForSingleObject(thread, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0) ExitProcess(3);
+    CloseHandle(thread);
+    return !failed;
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    LARGE_INTEGER freq, begin, end;
+    PRTL_CRITICAL_SECTION lock;
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_CS_MODE", "");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_CS_TRACE_CRT", "");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_CS_WATCH", "");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_CS_COUNTERS", argc > 1 && !strcmp(argv[1], "counters") ? "1" : "0");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_KERNEL_LOG_BUDGET", "0");
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 16 * 1024 * 1024,
+                          MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    start_event = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    if (!memory || !start_event) return 10;
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < COLLISIONS; i++)
+        memset(guest_lock(i), 0xA5, 32);
+    imports[0] = 0x80000000u | 306; /* TryEnter */
+    imports[1] = 0x80000000u | 294; /* Leave */
+    memcpy(memory + 0x600000, imports, sizeof imports);
+    xbox_kernel_set_thunk_address(0x600000, 2);
+    xbox_kernel_bridge_init();
+    memcpy(imports, memory + 0x600000, sizeof imports);
+
+    if (!run_workers(0) || shared_count != THREADS * SHARED_ITERATIONS ||
+        !run_workers(1)) return 1;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < COLLISIONS; i++)
+        if (collision_count[i] != THREADS * COLLISION_ITERATIONS) return 2;
+
+    lock = guest_lock(0);
+    xbox_RtlEnterCriticalSection(lock);
+    xbox_RtlEnterCriticalSection(lock);
+    if (!try_from_other_thread(0)) return 3;
+    xbox_RtlLeaveCriticalSection(lock);
+    if (!try_from_other_thread(0)) return 4;
+    xbox_RtlLeaveCriticalSection(lock);
+    /* Try+bridge Leave must free the same native shadow, on every thread. */
+    if (!try_from_other_thread(1) || !try_from_other_thread(1)) return 5;
+    if (invoke(0) != 1 || invoke(0) != 1) return 6;
+    xbox_RtlLeaveCriticalSection(lock);
+    if (!try_from_other_thread(0)) return 7;
+    xbox_RtlLeaveCriticalSection(lock);
+    if (!try_from_other_thread(1)) return 8;
+
+    QueryPerformanceFrequency(&freq);
+    QueryPerformanceCounter(&begin);
+    if (!run_workers(2)) return 9;
+    QueryPerformanceCounter(&end);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < COLLISIONS; i++)
+        for (unsigned j = 0; j < 32; j++)
+            if (((uint8_t *)guest_lock(i))[j] != 0xA5) return 11;
+    printf("PASS: lazy initialization, recursive exclusion, 40 colliding locks, "
+           "bridge Try/Leave and unchanged guest fields; %u independent lock pairs in %.2f ms\n",
+           THREADS * BENCH_ITERATIONS,
+           (end.QuadPart - begin.QuadPart) * 1000.0 / freq.QuadPart);
+    CloseHandle(start_event);
+    VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_dpc_exclusion_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_dpc_exclusion_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1fb8d98
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_dpc_exclusion_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+/* Synthetic guest DPCs exercise the real queue, timer and IRQL dispatcher. */
+#ifndef KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+#define KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE "../../src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c"
+#endif
+#include KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+/* A before-source comparison can supply the unmodified timer-loop body as
+ * this callable adapter; normal tests call the production helper directly. */
+#ifdef KERNEL_TIMER_CLAIM_ADAPTER
+#include KERNEL_TIMER_CLAIM_ADAPTER
+#endif
+
+#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "DPC exclusion check failed at line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #c); \
+    ExitProcess(1); \
+} } while (0)
+
+enum { DPC = 0x20000, TIMER = 0x22000, DPC_CONTEXT = 0x24000, ROUTINE = 0x26000 };
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static HANDLE worker_started;
+static volatile LONG callbacks;
+static int timer_mode;
+
+static void guest_dpc(void)
+{
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 2);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) == 0);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) == DPC);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 8) == DPC_CONTEXT);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 12) == (timer_mode ? 0 : 0x1234));
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 16) == (timer_mode ? 0 : 0x5678));
+    InterlockedIncrement(&callbacks);
+    g_esp += 20; /* Original guest DeferredRoutine stdcall ret 16. */
+}
+
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup(uint32_t address)
+{
+    return address == ROUTINE ? guest_dpc : NULL;
+}
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup_manual(uint32_t address)
+{
+    (void)address;
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+static void prepare(void)
+{
+    memset(memory + DPC, 0, 32);
+    BRIDGE_MEM16(DPC) = 0x13;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(DPC + 12) = ROUTINE;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(DPC + 16) = DPC_CONTEXT;
+    if (timer_mode) {
+        g_timers[0].timer_va = TIMER;
+        g_timers[0].dpc_va = DPC;
+        g_timers[0].due_ms = 0;
+        g_timers[0].period_ms = 0;
+    } else {
+        g_esp = 0x30000;
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) = DPC;
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) = 0x1234;
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 8) = 0x5678;
+        bridge_KeInsertQueueDpc();
+        CHECK(g_eax == 1 && BRIDGE_MEM8(DPC + 2) == 1);
+    }
+}
+
+static DWORD WINAPI drain(LPVOID unused)
+{
+    (void)unused;
+    g_esp = 0x80000;
+    g_fs_base = 0x18000;
+    CHECK(SetEvent(worker_started));
+    if (timer_mode) kernel_fire_due_timer(0, 1000);
+    else kernel_drain_dpcs();
+    CHECK(g_esp == 0x80000);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 0);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static HANDLE start_worker(void)
+{
+    CHECK(ResetEvent(worker_started));
+    HANDLE worker = CreateThread(NULL, 0, drain, NULL, 0, NULL);
+    CHECK(worker);
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(worker_started, 3000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    return worker;
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    timer_mode = argc > 1 && !strcmp(argv[1], "timer");
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 16 * 1024 * 1024,
+                          MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    CHECK(memory);
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory;
+    g_fs_base = 0x10000;
+    worker_started = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    CHECK(worker_started);
+    InitializeCriticalSection(&g_timer_lock);
+    g_timer_started = 1; /* Use an explicitly driven worker, not a poll thread. */
+
+    int saved_irql = xbox_IrqlEnterInterrupt(2);
+    prepare();
+    HANDLE worker = start_worker();
+    /* The processor belongs to this guest thread. A host worker must neither
+     * claim nor run deferred work until this thread restores its old IRQL. */
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(worker, 100) == WAIT_TIMEOUT);
+    CHECK(callbacks == 0);
+    if (timer_mode) {
+        EnterCriticalSection(&g_timer_lock);
+        int still_armed = g_timers[0].timer_va == TIMER;
+        LeaveCriticalSection(&g_timer_lock);
+        CHECK(still_armed);
+        CHECK(xbox_kernel_cancel_timer(TIMER) == 1);
+    } else {
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(DPC + 2) == 1);
+        g_esp = 0x30000;
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) = DPC;
+        bridge_KeRemoveQueueDpc();
+        CHECK(g_eax == 1 && BRIDGE_MEM8(DPC + 2) == 0);
+    }
+    xbox_IrqlLeaveInterrupt(saved_irql);
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(worker, 3000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(worker));
+    CHECK(callbacks == 0 && BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 0);
+
+    /* Uncancelled work still executes once, at the correct IRQL, with the
+     * original four guest arguments and stack cleanup. */
+    prepare();
+    worker = start_worker();
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(worker, 3000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(worker));
+    CHECK(callbacks == 1);
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(worker_started));
+    CHECK(VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    printf("PASS: %s claim obeys guest DISPATCH exclusion and cancellation; "
+           "uncancelled callback ABI preserved\n", timer_mode ? "timer" : "DPC");
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_dpc_lower_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_dpc_lower_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3376b37
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_dpc_lower_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,316 @@
+/* Queued completions must precede object destruction after KfLowerIrql. */
+#ifndef KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+#define KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE "../../src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c"
+#endif
+#define xbox_HeapAlloc test_dpc_heap_alloc
+#define xbox_HeapFree test_dpc_heap_free
+#include KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+#undef xbox_HeapAlloc
+#undef xbox_HeapFree
+#include <fenv.h>
+#include <xmmintrin.h>
+
+#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "DPC lowering check failed at line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #c); \
+    ExitProcess(1); \
+} } while (0)
+
+enum { DPC = 0x20000, HEAD = 0x22000, VOICE = 0x24000,
+       ROUTINE = 0x26000, LIVE_VTABLE = 0x362978, DEAD_VTABLE = 0x362910 };
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static int callbacks, max_depth;
+static RECOMP_TLS int callback_depth;
+static const char *mode;
+static RECOMP_TLS DWORD lowering_thread;
+static LONG fallback_allocations, fallback_frees;
+static uint32_t outer_callback_stack;
+static uint32_t callback_stack;
+static unsigned char caller_stack[256];
+
+/* Keep the focused harness's memory arena independent of heap initialization;
+ * production still allocates from xbox_HeapAlloc on worker-pool exhaustion. */
+uint32_t test_dpc_heap_alloc(uint32_t size, uint32_t alignment)
+{
+    CHECK(size == XBOX_WORKER_STACK_SIZE && alignment == 4096);
+    LONG index = InterlockedIncrement(&fallback_allocations) - 1;
+    return 0xC00000 + (uint32_t)index * XBOX_WORKER_STACK_SIZE;
+}
+void test_dpc_heap_free(uint32_t address)
+{
+    CHECK(address >= 0xC00000 && address < 0x1000000);
+    InterlockedIncrement(&fallback_frees);
+}
+static DWORD WINAPI parallel_lower(LPVOID unused);
+
+/* Avoid depending on declarations introduced by the repair, so the same
+ * regression compiles against a saved before-source. */
+extern RECOMP_TLS uint32_t g_ebp;
+extern RECOMP_TLS int g_df, g_fp_top, g_fp_cmp;
+extern RECOMP_TLS uint16_t g_fp_control_word, g_fp_cc;
+extern RECOMP_TLS double g_fp_stack[8];
+extern RECOMP_TLS RecompMmx g_mm0, g_mm1, g_mm2, g_mm3;
+extern RECOMP_TLS RecompMmx g_mm4, g_mm5, g_mm6, g_mm7;
+extern RECOMP_TLS RecompXmm g_xmm0, g_xmm1, g_xmm2, g_xmm3;
+extern RECOMP_TLS RecompXmm g_xmm4, g_xmm5, g_xmm6, g_xmm7;
+
+typedef struct {
+    uint32_t regs[10];
+    RecompMmx mm[8];
+    RecompXmm xmm[8];
+    double fp[8];
+    int df, fp_top, fp_cmp, host_rounding;
+    uint16_t control, cc;
+    unsigned mxcsr;
+} State;
+
+static void snapshot(State *s)
+{
+    memset(s, 0, sizeof(*s));
+    s->regs[0] = g_ecx; s->regs[1] = g_edx; s->regs[2] = g_esp;
+    s->regs[3] = g_ebx; s->regs[4] = g_esi; s->regs[5] = g_edi;
+    s->regs[6] = g_ebp; s->regs[7] = g_seh_ebp;
+    s->regs[8] = g_fs_base; s->regs[9] = g_xbox_kernel_caller;
+    s->mm[0] = g_mm0; s->mm[1] = g_mm1; s->mm[2] = g_mm2; s->mm[3] = g_mm3;
+    s->mm[4] = g_mm4; s->mm[5] = g_mm5; s->mm[6] = g_mm6; s->mm[7] = g_mm7;
+    s->xmm[0] = g_xmm0; s->xmm[1] = g_xmm1; s->xmm[2] = g_xmm2; s->xmm[3] = g_xmm3;
+    s->xmm[4] = g_xmm4; s->xmm[5] = g_xmm5; s->xmm[6] = g_xmm6; s->xmm[7] = g_xmm7;
+    memcpy(s->fp, g_fp_stack, sizeof(s->fp));
+    s->df = g_df; s->fp_top = g_fp_top; s->fp_cmp = g_fp_cmp;
+    s->control = g_fp_control_word; s->cc = g_fp_cc;
+    s->host_rounding = fegetround(); s->mxcsr = _mm_getcsr();
+}
+
+static void queue(void)
+{
+    uint32_t saved_esp = g_esp;
+    g_esp -= 12;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) = DPC;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) = 0x1234;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 8) = 0x5678;
+    bridge_KeInsertQueueDpc();
+    CHECK(g_eax == 1);
+    g_esp = saved_esp;
+}
+
+static void clobber_state(void)
+{
+    g_eax = g_ecx = g_edx = g_ebx = g_esi = g_edi = 0xDEADBEEF;
+    g_ebp = 0xDDDDDDDD; g_seh_ebp = 0xEEEEEEEE;
+    g_xbox_kernel_caller = 0xBADCA11;
+    memset(g_fp_stack, 0xBA, sizeof(g_fp_stack));
+    g_fp_top = 7; g_fp_cmp = -1; g_fp_control_word = 0x77F; g_fp_cc = 0x100;
+    g_mm0.q = g_mm1.q = g_mm2.q = g_mm3.q = 0xBAADF00DDEADBEEFull;
+    g_mm4 = g_mm5 = g_mm6 = g_mm7 = g_mm0;
+    g_xmm0.q[0] = 0xBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBBull; g_xmm0.q[1] = 0xCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCCull;
+    g_xmm1 = g_xmm2 = g_xmm3 = g_xmm4 = g_xmm5 = g_xmm6 = g_xmm7 = g_xmm0;
+    g_df = 1;
+    CHECK(fesetround(FE_TOWARDZERO) == 0);
+    _mm_setcsr(_mm_getcsr() ^ 0x8040u); /* FTZ and DAZ must also survive. */
+}
+
+static void guest_dpc(void)
+{
+    CHECK(GetCurrentThreadId() == lowering_thread);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + XBOX_KPCR_IRQL_OFFSET) == 2);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) == 0);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) == DPC);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 8) == VOICE);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 12) == 0x1234);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 16) == 0x5678);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(DPC + 2) == 0);
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "stack") || !strcmp(mode, "exhausted")) {
+        /* Match the observed USB alias: the request lies 0x54 bytes below
+         * the lowering caller's ESP, and a callback pushes a return PC there. */
+        uint32_t saved_esp = g_esp;
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 48; i++) {
+            g_esp -= 4;
+            BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) = 0x0035FBD3;
+        }
+        g_esp = saved_esp;
+        if (BRIDGE_MEM32(0x80000 - 0x54 + 8) != 0x5A5A5A5A)
+            fprintf(stderr, "USB-shaped request callback overwritten: %08X\n",
+                    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x80000 - 0x54 + 8));
+        CHECK(!memcmp(memory + 0x80000 - sizeof(caller_stack),
+                      caller_stack, sizeof(caller_stack)));
+        if (!strcmp(mode, "stack")) {
+            if (callback_stack) CHECK(callback_stack == g_esp);
+            callback_stack = g_esp;
+        }
+    }
+    callbacks++;
+    callback_depth++;
+    if (callback_depth > max_depth) max_depth = callback_depth;
+
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "context") || !strcmp(mode, "active")) {
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + XBOX_KPCR_DPC_ACTIVE_OFFSET) == 1);
+        bridge_KeIsExecutingDpc();
+        CHECK(g_eax == 1);
+    }
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "lifetime")) {
+        /* Match DirectSound's intrusive +0x54 completion link and the vtable
+         * transition at the end of its base destructor. */
+        uint32_t entry = BRIDGE_MEM32(HEAD);
+        CHECK(entry == VOICE + 0x54);
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(entry - 0x54) == LIVE_VTABLE);
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(HEAD) = BRIDGE_MEM32(HEAD + 4) = HEAD;
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(entry) = BRIDGE_MEM32(entry + 4) = entry;
+    } else if (!strcmp(mode, "context")) {
+        CHECK(g_df == 0);
+        clobber_state();
+    } else if (!strcmp(mode, "concurrent") && callbacks == 1) {
+        outer_callback_stack = g_esp;
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp - 64) = 0x12345678;
+        xbox_KfLowerIrql(0);
+        HANDLE thread = CreateThread(NULL, 0, parallel_lower, NULL, 0, NULL);
+        CHECK(thread && WaitForSingleObject(thread, 5000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+        CloseHandle(thread);
+        xbox_KfRaiseIrql(2);
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp - 64) == 0x12345678);
+    } else if (!strcmp(mode, "concurrent")) {
+        CHECK(g_esp != outer_callback_stack);
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp - 64) = 0xBAADF00D;
+    } else if (!strcmp(mode, "nested") && callbacks == 1) {
+        queue();
+        g_ecx = 0;
+        bridge_KfLowerIrql();
+        CHECK(callbacks == 1); /* Never invoke a DPC from inside a DPC. */
+        xbox_KfRaiseIrql(2);
+    }
+    callback_depth--;
+    g_esp += 20;
+}
+
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup(uint32_t address)
+{
+    return address == ROUTINE ? guest_dpc : NULL;
+}
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup_manual(uint32_t address)
+{
+    (void)address;
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+static void prepare(void)
+{
+    memset(memory + DPC, 0, 32);
+    BRIDGE_MEM16(DPC) = 0x13;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(DPC + 12) = ROUTINE;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(DPC + 16) = VOICE;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(VOICE) = LIVE_VTABLE;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(HEAD) = BRIDGE_MEM32(HEAD + 4) = VOICE + 0x54;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(VOICE + 0x54) = BRIDGE_MEM32(VOICE + 0x58) = HEAD;
+    queue();
+}
+
+static DWORD WINAPI parallel_lower(LPVOID unused)
+{
+    (void)unused;
+    g_fs_base = 0x11000; g_esp = 0x90000;
+    lowering_thread = GetCurrentThreadId();
+    xbox_KfRaiseIrql(2); prepare();
+    g_ecx = 0; bridge_KfLowerIrql();
+    CHECK(g_esp == 0x90000);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    CHECK(argc == 2);
+    mode = argv[1];
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 16 * 1024 * 1024,
+                          MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    CHECK(memory);
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory;
+    g_fs_base = 0x10000;
+    g_esp = 0x80000;
+    lowering_thread = GetCurrentThreadId();
+    int occupied[XBOX_WORKER_STACK_COUNT];
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "exhausted") || !strcmp(mode, "concurrent")) {
+        for (int i = 0; i < XBOX_WORKER_STACK_COUNT; i++) {
+            occupied[i] = xbox_worker_stack_alloc();
+            CHECK(occupied[i] >= 0);
+        }
+        CHECK(xbox_worker_stack_alloc() < 0);
+    }
+    xbox_KfRaiseIrql(16);
+    prepare();
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "stack") || !strcmp(mode, "exhausted")) {
+        memset(caller_stack, 0x5A, sizeof(caller_stack));
+        memcpy(memory + 0x80000 - sizeof(caller_stack), caller_stack, sizeof(caller_stack));
+    }
+
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "boundary")) {
+        g_ecx = 2;
+        bridge_KfLowerIrql();
+        CHECK(callbacks == 0 && BRIDGE_MEM8(DPC + 2) == 1);
+    }
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "context")) {
+        const int modes[] = { FE_TONEAREST, FE_DOWNWARD, FE_UPWARD, FE_TOWARDZERO };
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(modes) / sizeof(modes[0]); i++) {
+            if (i) { xbox_KfRaiseIrql(2); prepare(); }
+            g_ecx = 0; g_edx = 0x22222222; g_ebx = 0x33333333;
+            g_esi = 0x44444444; g_edi = 0x55555555;
+            g_ebp = 0x66666666; g_seh_ebp = 0x77777777; g_xbox_kernel_caller = 0x88888888;
+            memset(g_fp_stack, 0x12, sizeof(g_fp_stack));
+            g_fp_top = 3; g_fp_cmp = 1; g_fp_control_word = 0xB7F; g_fp_cc = 0x4000;
+            RecompMmx *mm[] = { &g_mm0, &g_mm1, &g_mm2, &g_mm3, &g_mm4, &g_mm5, &g_mm6, &g_mm7 };
+            RecompXmm *xmm[] = { &g_xmm0, &g_xmm1, &g_xmm2, &g_xmm3, &g_xmm4, &g_xmm5, &g_xmm6, &g_xmm7 };
+            for (unsigned r = 0; r < 8; r++) {
+                mm[r]->q = 0x1234567800000000ull + r;
+                xmm[r]->q[0] = 0x9988776600000000ull + r;
+                xmm[r]->q[1] = 0xAABBCCDD00000000ull + r;
+            }
+            g_df = 1;
+            CHECK(fesetround(modes[i]) == 0);
+            _mm_setcsr((_mm_getcsr() & ~0x8040u) | ((i & 1) ? 0x8040u : 0));
+            State before, after;
+            snapshot(&before);
+            bridge_KfLowerIrql();
+            snapshot(&after);
+            CHECK(callbacks == (int)i + 1);
+            CHECK(g_eax == 0 && !memcmp(&before, &after, sizeof(before)));
+        }
+    } else {
+        g_ecx = 0;
+        bridge_KfLowerIrql();
+        CHECK(callbacks == ((!strcmp(mode, "nested") || !strcmp(mode, "concurrent")) ? 2 : 1));
+    }
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "stack") || !strcmp(mode, "exhausted")) {
+        CHECK(!memcmp(memory + 0x80000 - sizeof(caller_stack), caller_stack, sizeof(caller_stack)));
+        CHECK(g_esp == 0x80000);
+        if (!strcmp(mode, "exhausted")) {
+            CHECK(fallback_allocations == 1);
+            xbox_KfRaiseIrql(2); prepare();
+            memcpy(memory + 0x80000 - sizeof(caller_stack), caller_stack, sizeof(caller_stack));
+            g_ecx = 0; bridge_KfLowerIrql();
+            CHECK(callbacks == 2 && fallback_allocations == 2 && fallback_frees == 2);
+            for (int i = 0; i < XBOX_WORKER_STACK_COUNT; i++) xbox_worker_stack_free(occupied[i]);
+        }
+        /* Every lease must be released after a synchronous drain. */
+        for (int i = 0; i < XBOX_WORKER_STACK_COUNT; i++) {
+            occupied[i] = xbox_worker_stack_alloc(); CHECK(occupied[i] >= 0);
+        }
+        for (int i = 0; i < XBOX_WORKER_STACK_COUNT; i++) xbox_worker_stack_free(occupied[i]);
+    }
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "concurrent")) {
+        CHECK(fallback_allocations == 2 && fallback_frees == 2);
+        for (int i = 0; i < XBOX_WORKER_STACK_COUNT; i++) xbox_worker_stack_free(occupied[i]);
+    }
+    CHECK(max_depth == 1 && g_esp == 0x80000);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + XBOX_KPCR_IRQL_OFFSET) == 0);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + XBOX_KPCR_DPC_ACTIVE_OFFSET) == 0);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(DPC + 2) == 0);
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "lifetime")) {
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(VOICE) = DEAD_VTABLE;
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(HEAD) == HEAD);
+    }
+    int completed = callbacks;
+    kernel_drain_dpcs();
+    CHECK(callbacks == completed); /* Worker fallback cannot run it twice. */
+    bridge_KeIsExecutingDpc();
+    CHECK(g_eax == 0);
+    CHECK(xbox_IrqlRaisedCount() == 0);
+    CHECK(VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    printf("PASS: DPC lower %s\n", mode);
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_dpc_queue_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_dpc_queue_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3324b1e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_dpc_queue_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+/* Canceled DPCs must release queue capacity without disturbing live order. */
+#ifndef KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+#define KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE "../../src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c"
+#endif
+#include KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { fprintf(stderr, "DPC queue line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #c); ExitProcess(1); } } while (0)
+enum { DPC_BASE = 0x20000, ROUTINE = 0x26000 };
+static unsigned seen[128], calls;
+static void guest_dpc(void)
+{
+    unsigned id = (BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) - DPC_BASE) / 32;
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 2);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 12) == id + 100);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 16) == id + 200);
+    CHECK(!BRIDGE_MEM8(DPC_BASE + id * 32 + 2));
+    CHECK(calls < 128); seen[calls++] = id;
+    g_esp += 20;
+}
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup(uint32_t address) { return address == ROUTINE ? guest_dpc : NULL; }
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup_manual(uint32_t address) { (void)address; return NULL; }
+static void insert(unsigned id, unsigned result)
+{
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) = DPC_BASE + id * 32;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) = id + 100;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 8) = id + 200;
+    bridge_KeInsertQueueDpc(); CHECK(g_eax == result);
+}
+static void remove_dpc(unsigned id, unsigned result)
+{
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) = DPC_BASE + id * 32;
+    bridge_KeRemoveQueueDpc(); CHECK(g_eax == result);
+}
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    uint8_t *memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 16 * 1024 * 1024, MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    unsigned i;
+    int saved;
+    CHECK(memory && argc == 2);
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory; g_fs_base = 0x10000; g_esp = 0x80000;
+    for (i = 0; i < 64; i++) BRIDGE_MEM32(DPC_BASE + i * 32 + 12) = ROUTINE;
+    saved = xbox_IrqlEnterInterrupt(2);
+    if (!strcmp(argv[1], "capacity")) {
+        for (i = 0; i < 1000; i++) { insert(0, 1); remove_dpc(0, 1); }
+        insert(1, 1);
+        xbox_IrqlLeaveInterrupt(saved);
+        kernel_drain_dpcs(); CHECK(calls == 1 && seen[0] == 1);
+    } else {
+        g_dpc_head = g_dpc_tail = XBOX_MAX_PENDING_DPC - 3;
+        for (i = 1; i <= 5; i++) insert(i, 1);
+        remove_dpc(3, 1); remove_dpc(1, 1); remove_dpc(5, 1);
+        remove_dpc(3, 0); insert(6, 1); insert(2, 0);
+        xbox_IrqlLeaveInterrupt(saved);
+        kernel_drain_dpcs();
+        CHECK(calls == 3 && seen[0] == 2 && seen[1] == 4 && seen[2] == 6);
+        CHECK(g_dpc_head == g_dpc_tail);
+    }
+    CHECK(g_esp == 0x80000 && BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 0);
+    VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
+    printf("PASS DPC %s: cancellation releases capacity; live order, arguments and duplicate rejection preserved\n", argv[1]);
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_file_sharing_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_file_sharing_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..acfb81a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_file_sharing_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,265 @@
+/* A real host sharing conflict must survive the Xbox error conversion. */
+#include "kernel.h"
+#include "xbox_memory_layout.h"
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <io.h>
+
+typedef void (*guest_fn)(void);
+extern guest_fn recomp_lookup_kernel(uint32_t);
+extern RECOMP_TLS uint32_t g_eax, g_esp;
+extern ptrdiff_t g_xbox_mem_offset;
+extern uint32_t xbox_LastFileError(void);
+void *recomp_lookup(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+void *recomp_lookup_manual(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+
+typedef struct MissingOpen {
+    HANDLE root, ready, release;
+    NTSTATUS status, ios_status;
+    ULONG_PTR information;
+    uint32_t error_before, error_after;
+} MissingOpen;
+
+static DWORD WINAPI missing_open_worker(void *parameter)
+{
+    MissingOpen *test = parameter;
+    XBOX_ANSI_STRING name = {0};
+    XBOX_OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES oa = {0};
+    XBOX_IO_STATUS_BLOCK ios = {0};
+    HANDLE opened = NULL;
+    name.Buffer = "absent.bin";
+    name.Length = (USHORT)strlen(name.Buffer);
+    name.MaximumLength = name.Length + 1;
+    oa.RootDirectory = test->root;
+    oa.ObjectName = &name;
+    test->status = xbox_NtCreateFile(&opened, XBOX_GENERIC_READ, &oa, &ios,
+        NULL, 0x80, 1, XBOX_FILE_OPEN, XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE);
+    test->ios_status = ios.Status;
+    test->information = ios.Information;
+    test->error_before = xbox_LastFileError();
+    SetEvent(test->ready);
+    if (WaitForSingleObject(test->release, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0) return 2;
+    test->error_after = xbox_LastFileError();
+    if (opened) xbox_NtClose(opened);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static int malformed_name_contract(guest_fn open_guest, uint8_t *memory)
+{
+    uint32_t *sp = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x20000);
+    FILE *capture = NULL;
+    int saved_stderr, ok;
+    char output[4096] = {0};
+    if (!open_guest || tmpfile_s(&capture) || !capture) return 0;
+    saved_stderr = _dup(_fileno(stderr));
+    if (saved_stderr < 0) { fclose(capture); return 0; }
+    fflush(stderr);
+    if (_dup2(_fileno(capture), _fileno(stderr))) {
+        _close(saved_stderr); fclose(capture); return 0;
+    }
+    memset(sp, 0, 40);
+    memset(memory + 0x40000, 0, 0x110);
+    *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x40004) = 0x40100; /* Empty ANSI_STRING.Buffer. */
+    *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x40500) = 0xA5A5A5A5;
+    sp[0] = 0xBEEF0001; sp[1] = 0x40500; sp[2] = XBOX_GENERIC_READ;
+    sp[3] = 0x40000; sp[4] = 0x40600;
+    sp[6] = 0x80; sp[7] = 1; sp[8] = XBOX_FILE_OPEN; sp[9] = XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE;
+    g_esp = 0x20000;
+    open_guest();
+    fflush(stderr);
+    _dup2(saved_stderr, _fileno(stderr));
+    _close(saved_stderr);
+    rewind(capture);
+    fread(output, 1, sizeof output - 1, capture);
+    fclose(capture);
+    ok = g_eax == STATUS_OBJECT_PATH_NOT_FOUND && g_esp == 0x20028 &&
+         *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x40600) == STATUS_OBJECT_PATH_NOT_FOUND &&
+         *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x40604) == 0 &&
+         *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x40500) == 0xA5A5A5A5 &&
+         strstr(output, "win32 err=0") && !strstr(output, "ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION");
+    if (!ok) fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: malformed guest name inherited an unrelated host open error:\n%s", output);
+    return ok;
+}
+
+/* System-link instances may share guest read-only opens, including a guest
+ * ShareAccess of zero. That exception must never give writers shared access. */
+static int shared_read_contract(XBOX_OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES *oa)
+{
+    HANDLE first = NULL, second = NULL, writer = NULL;
+    XBOX_IO_STATUS_BLOCK ios = {0};
+    NTSTATUS status;
+    int ok = 0;
+    status = xbox_NtCreateFile(&first, XBOX_GENERIC_READ, oa, &ios,
+        NULL, 0x80, 0, XBOX_FILE_OPEN, XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE);
+    if (status != STATUS_SUCCESS || !first) goto done;
+    status = xbox_NtCreateFile(&second, XBOX_GENERIC_READ, oa, &ios,
+        NULL, 0x80, 0, XBOX_FILE_OPEN, XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE);
+    if (status != STATUS_SUCCESS || !second) goto done;
+    status = xbox_NtCreateFile(&writer, XBOX_GENERIC_WRITE, oa, &ios,
+        NULL, 0x80, 1, XBOX_FILE_OPEN, XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE);
+    if (status != STATUS_SHARING_VIOLATION || ios.Status != status || writer ||
+        xbox_LastFileError() != ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION) goto done;
+    xbox_NtClose(second); second = NULL;
+    xbox_NtClose(first); first = NULL;
+    status = xbox_NtCreateFile(&writer, XBOX_GENERIC_WRITE, oa, &ios,
+        NULL, 0x80, 0, XBOX_FILE_OPEN, XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE);
+    if (status != STATUS_SUCCESS || !writer) goto done;
+    status = xbox_NtCreateFile(&first, XBOX_GENERIC_READ, oa, &ios,
+        NULL, 0x80, 0, XBOX_FILE_OPEN, XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE);
+    ok = status == STATUS_SHARING_VIOLATION && ios.Status == status && !first &&
+         xbox_LastFileError() == ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION;
+done:
+    if (first) xbox_NtClose(first);
+    if (second) xbox_NtClose(second);
+    if (writer) xbox_NtClose(writer);
+    if (!ok) fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: system-link shared reads or exclusive writes changed\n");
+    return ok;
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+    wchar_t base[MAX_PATH], dir[MAX_PATH] = {0}, path[MAX_PATH] = {0};
+    HANDLE exclusive = INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE, root = INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE, opened = NULL;
+    XBOX_ANSI_STRING name;
+    XBOX_OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES oa;
+    XBOX_IO_STATUS_BLOCK ios;
+    NTSTATUS status;
+    uint8_t *memory = NULL;
+    guest_fn convert;
+    int result = 1, directory_created = 0;
+    uint32_t *sp;
+    MissingOpen missing = {0};
+    HANDLE worker = NULL;
+
+    if (!GetTempPathW(MAX_PATH, base) ||
+        !GetTempFileNameW(base, L"xfs", 0, dir))
+        goto done;
+    if (!DeleteFileW(dir) || !CreateDirectoryW(dir, NULL))
+        goto done;
+    directory_created = 1;
+    if (swprintf_s(path, MAX_PATH, L"%s\\sharing.bin", dir) < 0)
+        goto done;
+    exclusive = CreateFileW(path, GENERIC_READ | GENERIC_WRITE, 0, NULL,
+                            CREATE_NEW, FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL, NULL);
+    root = CreateFileW(dir, FILE_LIST_DIRECTORY, FILE_SHARE_READ | FILE_SHARE_WRITE | FILE_SHARE_DELETE,
+                       NULL, OPEN_EXISTING, FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS, NULL);
+    if (exclusive == INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE || root == INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE)
+        goto done;
+    memset(&name, 0, sizeof name);
+    name.Buffer = "sharing.bin";
+    name.Length = (USHORT)strlen(name.Buffer);
+    name.MaximumLength = name.Length + 1;
+    memset(&oa, 0, sizeof oa);
+    oa.RootDirectory = root;
+    oa.ObjectName = &name;
+    memset(&ios, 0xA5, sizeof ios);
+    status = xbox_NtCreateFile(&opened,
+        XBOX_GENERIC_READ | XBOX_SYNCHRONIZE | XBOX_FILE_READ_ATTRIBUTES,
+        &oa, &ios, NULL, 0x80, 1, XBOX_FILE_OPEN,
+        XBOX_FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_NONALERT | XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE);
+    if (status != STATUS_SHARING_VIOLATION || ios.Status != status ||
+        ios.Information != 0 || opened != NULL ||
+        xbox_RtlNtStatusToDosError(status) != ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: sharing conflict status=%08X ios=%08X information=%llu handle=%p\n",
+                (unsigned)status, (unsigned)ios.Status,
+                (unsigned long long)ios.Information, opened);
+        goto done;
+    }
+
+    /* Another streaming worker can miss an optional search candidate between
+     * the host open and the bridge's diagnostic. Each thread must retain its
+     * own error; the missing open must still fail with its exact status. */
+    missing.root = root;
+    missing.ready = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    missing.release = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    if (!missing.ready || !missing.release) goto done;
+    worker = CreateThread(NULL, 0, missing_open_worker, &missing, 0, NULL);
+    if (!worker || WaitForSingleObject(missing.ready, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0) goto done;
+    if (xbox_LastFileError() != ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION ||
+        missing.status != STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_NOT_FOUND || missing.ios_status != missing.status ||
+        missing.information || missing.error_before != ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: concurrent open mixed error provenance: main=%u worker=%u status=%08X\n",
+                xbox_LastFileError(), missing.error_before, (unsigned)missing.status);
+        goto done;
+    }
+
+    /* Translated games use the bridge's independent status mapping. */
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 16 * 1024 * 1024,
+                          MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    if (!memory)
+        goto done;
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory;
+    *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x10000) = 0x80000000u | 301;
+    *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x10004) = 0x80000000u | 190;
+    xbox_kernel_set_thunk_address(0x10000, 2);
+    xbox_kernel_bridge_init();
+    convert = recomp_lookup_kernel(*(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x10000));
+    if (!convert)
+        goto done;
+    g_esp = 0x20000;
+    sp = (uint32_t *)(memory + g_esp);
+    sp[0] = 0xBEEF0001;
+    sp[1] = (uint32_t)status;
+    convert();
+    if (g_eax != ERROR_SHARING_VIOLATION || g_esp != 0x20008) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: bridge lost sharing error: eax=%08X esp=%08X\n", g_eax, g_esp);
+        goto done;
+    }
+    if (!malformed_name_contract(recomp_lookup_kernel(*(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x10004)), memory))
+        goto done;
+
+    /* Sharing was enforced, and the same request can succeed after release. */
+    CloseHandle(exclusive);
+    exclusive = INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE;
+    status = xbox_NtCreateFile(&opened,
+        XBOX_GENERIC_READ | XBOX_SYNCHRONIZE | XBOX_FILE_READ_ATTRIBUTES,
+        &oa, &ios, NULL, 0x80, 1, XBOX_FILE_OPEN,
+        XBOX_FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_NONALERT | XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE);
+    if (status != STATUS_SUCCESS || ios.Status != STATUS_SUCCESS || !opened) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: unchanged open failed after host lock closed: %08X\n", (unsigned)status);
+        goto done;
+    }
+    if (xbox_LastFileError() != 0) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: successful open retained a stale failure reason\n");
+        goto done;
+    }
+    SetEvent(missing.release);
+    if (WaitForSingleObject(worker, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0 ||
+        missing.error_after != ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND || xbox_LastFileError() != 0) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: worker lost its error after the other thread opened successfully\n");
+        goto done;
+    }
+    /* Empty-file streaming completion remains EOF, not successful fake data. */
+    {
+        unsigned char bytes[512];
+        LARGE_INTEGER offset = {0};
+        memset(bytes, 0xA5, sizeof bytes);
+        status = xbox_NtReadFile(opened, NULL, NULL, NULL, &ios, bytes, sizeof bytes, &offset);
+        if (status != STATUS_END_OF_FILE || ios.Status != status || ios.Information != 0 || bytes[0] != 0xA5) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: EOF changed status, count or destination bytes\n");
+            goto done;
+        }
+    }
+    xbox_NtClose(opened); opened = NULL;
+    if (!shared_read_contract(&oa)) goto done;
+    puts("PASS: system-link reads share; writes and host locks stay exclusive; concurrent errors, absence and EOF retain native statuses");
+    result = 0;
+
+done:
+    if (worker) {
+        SetEvent(missing.release);
+        WaitForSingleObject(worker, 5000);
+        CloseHandle(worker);
+    }
+    if (missing.ready) CloseHandle(missing.ready);
+    if (missing.release) CloseHandle(missing.release);
+    if (opened && opened != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE) xbox_NtClose(opened);
+    if (root != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE) CloseHandle(root);
+    if (exclusive != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE) CloseHandle(exclusive);
+    if (memory) VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
+    if (*path) DeleteFileW(path);
+    if (directory_created) RemoveDirectoryW(dir);
+    return result;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_handle_thread_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_handle_thread_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..95ff65e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_handle_thread_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,327 @@
+/* Real event/file imports share the bridge's actual private handle table. */
+#include "../../src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c"
+
+#define WORKERS 12
+#define ROUNDS 32
+#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: line %d: %s (error %lu)\n", __LINE__, #c, GetLastError()); \
+    exit(1); \
+} } while (0)
+
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup(uint32_t address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup_manual(uint32_t address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+
+enum { CLOSE, CREATE_EVENT, CREATE_FILE, READ_FILE, SET_EVENT, WAIT_EVENT, WRITE_FILE, SERVICES };
+static const uint32_t ordinals[SERVICES] = {187, 189, 190, 219, 225, 233, 236};
+static uint32_t services[SERVICES];
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static uint32_t root_token;
+static wchar_t directory[MAX_PATH];
+
+typedef struct {
+    CRITICAL_SECTION lock;
+    CONDITION_VARIABLE changed;
+    unsigned count, generation;
+} barrier_t;
+static barrier_t barrier;
+
+static void rendezvous(void)
+{
+    unsigned generation;
+    EnterCriticalSection(&barrier.lock);
+    generation = barrier.generation;
+    if (++barrier.count == WORKERS + 1) {
+        barrier.count = 0;
+        barrier.generation++;
+        WakeAllConditionVariable(&barrier.changed);
+    } else {
+        while (generation == barrier.generation)
+            CHECK(SleepConditionVariableCS(&barrier.changed, &barrier.lock, 10000));
+    }
+    LeaveCriticalSection(&barrier.lock);
+}
+
+static uint32_t invoke(unsigned service, uint32_t stack, const uint32_t *args, unsigned count)
+{
+    recomp_func_t fn;
+    uint32_t *sp = (uint32_t *)(memory + stack);
+    sp[0] = 0xBEEF0001;
+    memcpy(sp + 1, args, count * sizeof *args);
+    g_esp = stack;
+    fn = recomp_lookup_kernel(services[service]);
+    CHECK(fn != NULL);
+    fn();
+    CHECK(g_esp == stack + 4 + count * 4);
+    return g_eax;
+}
+
+static uint32_t arena(unsigned id) { return 0x20000 + id * 0x1000; }
+static uint32_t guest_word(uint32_t va) { return *(uint32_t *)(memory + va); }
+
+static void close_token(uint32_t token, uint32_t stack)
+{
+    CHECK(invoke(CLOSE, stack, &token, 1) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+}
+
+static void file_name(unsigned id, unsigned round, char *name, size_t bytes)
+{
+    CHECK(sprintf_s(name, bytes, "worker-%02u-%02u.bin", id, round) > 0);
+}
+
+static void delete_file(unsigned id, unsigned round)
+{
+    char name[40];
+    wchar_t path[MAX_PATH];
+    file_name(id, round, name, sizeof name);
+    CHECK(swprintf_s(path, MAX_PATH, L"%s\\%hs", directory, name) > 0);
+    CHECK(DeleteFileW(path));
+}
+
+static void open_pair(unsigned id, unsigned round, uint32_t *event_token, uint32_t *file_token)
+{
+    uint32_t base = arena(id);
+    uint32_t event_args[] = {base + 0x100, 0, 0, 0};
+    uint32_t file_args[] = {base + 0x104,
+        XBOX_GENERIC_READ | XBOX_GENERIC_WRITE | XBOX_SYNCHRONIZE,
+        base + 0x160, base + 0x120, 0, 0, 0, XBOX_FILE_CREATE,
+        XBOX_FILE_SYNCHRONOUS_IO_NONALERT | XBOX_FILE_NON_DIRECTORY_FILE};
+    uint32_t io_args[] = {0, 0, 0, 0, base + 0x120, base + 0x280, 32, base + 0x300};
+    uint32_t *oa = (uint32_t *)(memory + base + 0x160);
+    uint16_t *name = (uint16_t *)(memory + base + 0x190);
+    uint32_t *payload = (uint32_t *)(memory + base + 0x280);
+    unsigned j;
+    char *filename = (char *)(memory + base + 0x200);
+    file_name(id, round, filename, 64);
+    memset(oa, 0, 12);
+    oa[0] = root_token;
+    oa[1] = base + 0x190;
+    name[0] = (uint16_t)strlen(filename);
+    name[1] = name[0] + 1;
+    *(uint32_t *)(name + 2) = base + 0x200;
+    *(uint64_t *)(memory + base + 0x300) = 0;
+    CHECK(invoke(CREATE_EVENT, base, event_args, 4) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+    *event_token = guest_word(base + 0x100);
+    CHECK(invoke(CREATE_FILE, base, file_args, 9) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+    *file_token = guest_word(base + 0x104);
+    CHECK(*event_token && *file_token && *event_token != *file_token);
+    for (j = 0; j < 8; ++j) payload[j] = 0xCA000000u | id << 16 | round << 8 | j;
+    io_args[0] = *file_token;
+    CHECK(invoke(WRITE_FILE, base, io_args, 8) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+    CHECK(guest_word(base + 0x124) == 32);
+    io_args[5] = base + 0x2A0;
+    memset(memory + base + 0x2A0, 0, 32);
+    CHECK(invoke(READ_FILE, base, io_args, 8) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+    CHECK(guest_word(base + 0x124) == 32);
+    CHECK(memcmp(memory + base + 0x280, memory + base + 0x2A0, 32) == 0);
+}
+
+static DWORD WINAPI io_worker(LPVOID parameter)
+{
+    unsigned id = (unsigned)(uintptr_t)parameter, round;
+    uint32_t event_token = 0, file_token = 0;
+    for (round = 0; round < ROUNDS; ++round) {
+        uint32_t next_event, next_file;
+        rendezvous();
+        /* Half the workers create before closing their previous pair. The
+         * other half close first, so registrations and takes overlap on
+         * distinct live objects without racing an object's own native use.
+         */
+        if (round && (id & 1)) {
+            close_token(event_token, arena(id));
+            close_token(file_token, arena(id));
+            delete_file(id, round - 1);
+        }
+        open_pair(id, round, &next_event, &next_file);
+        if (round && !(id & 1)) {
+            close_token(event_token, arena(id));
+            close_token(file_token, arena(id));
+            delete_file(id, round - 1);
+        }
+        event_token = next_event;
+        file_token = next_file;
+        rendezvous();
+        rendezvous();
+    }
+    rendezvous();
+    close_token(event_token, arena(id));
+    close_token(file_token, arena(id));
+    delete_file(id, ROUNDS - 1);
+    rendezvous();
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static void check_live_pairs(void)
+{
+    uint32_t tokens[WORKERS * 2];
+    HANDLE handles[WORKERS * 2];
+    unsigned i, j;
+    for (i = 0; i < WORKERS * 2; ++i) {
+        uint32_t va = arena(i / 2) + 0x100 + (i & 1) * 4;
+        DWORD flags;
+        tokens[i] = guest_word(va);
+        handles[i] = bridge_read_handle(va);
+        CHECK((tokens[i] & 0xFF000000u) == BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG);
+        CHECK(handles[i] && handles[i] == bridge_resolve_handle(tokens[i]));
+        CHECK(GetHandleInformation(handles[i], &flags));
+        for (j = 0; j < i; ++j)
+            CHECK(tokens[i] != tokens[j] && handles[i] != handles[j]);
+    }
+    /* Signal one guest event at a time, and observe all events through real
+     * wait imports. A token collision cannot pass this identity check.
+     */
+    *(uint64_t *)(memory + 0x100300) = 0;
+    for (i = 0; i < WORKERS; ++i) {
+        uint32_t set_args[] = {tokens[i * 2], 0};
+        CHECK(invoke(SET_EVENT, 0x100000, set_args, 2) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+        for (j = 0; j < WORKERS; ++j) {
+            uint32_t wait_args[] = {tokens[j * 2], 0, 0x100300};
+            CHECK(invoke(WAIT_EVENT, 0x100000, wait_args, 3) ==
+                  (j <= i ? STATUS_SUCCESS : STATUS_TIMEOUT));
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+static HANDLE shared_handle;
+static uint32_t shared_token, results[WORKERS];
+static HANDLE taken[WORKERS];
+static int take_mode;
+static DWORD WINAPI same_handle_worker(LPVOID parameter)
+{
+    unsigned id = (unsigned)(uintptr_t)parameter;
+    rendezvous();
+    if (take_mode) taken[id] = bridge_take_handle(shared_token);
+    else results[id] = bridge_handle_token(shared_handle);
+    rendezvous();
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static void same_handle_cohort(int taking)
+{
+    HANDLE threads[WORKERS];
+    unsigned i, winners = 0;
+    take_mode = taking;
+    for (i = 0; i < WORKERS; ++i) {
+        threads[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, same_handle_worker, (LPVOID)(uintptr_t)i, 0, NULL);
+        CHECK(threads[i]);
+    }
+    rendezvous();
+    rendezvous();
+    CHECK(WaitForMultipleObjects(WORKERS, threads, TRUE, 10000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    for (i = 0; i < WORKERS; ++i) {
+        if (taking) {
+            CHECK(taken[i] == NULL || taken[i] == shared_handle);
+            winners += taken[i] != NULL;
+        } else CHECK(results[i] == shared_token);
+        CHECK(CloseHandle(threads[i]));
+    }
+    if (taking) CHECK(winners == 1 && bridge_resolve_handle(shared_token) == NULL);
+}
+
+static void table_edges(void)
+{
+    uint32_t invalid[] = {BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG, BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG | BRIDGE_HANDLE_MAX,
+                          BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG | BRIDGE_HANDLE_MASK};
+    HANDLE wide = (HANDLE)(uintptr_t)UINT64_C(0x123456780000);
+    HANDLE overflow;
+    DWORD flags;
+    unsigned i;
+    uint32_t token;
+    CHECK(bridge_handle_token(NULL) == 0 && bridge_handle_token(INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE) == 0);
+    token = bridge_handle_token(wide);
+    CHECK(token == (BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG | 1));
+    CHECK(bridge_handle_token(wide) == token && bridge_resolve_handle(token) == wide);
+    bridge_write_handle(0x18000, wide);
+    CHECK(guest_word(0x18000) == token && bridge_read_handle(0x18000) == wide);
+    CHECK(bridge_take_handle(token) == wide && bridge_take_handle(token) == NULL);
+    CHECK(bridge_resolve_handle(0xFFFFFFFEu) == (HANDLE)(intptr_t)-2);
+    CHECK(bridge_resolve_handle(0xFFFFFFFFu) == (HANDLE)(intptr_t)-1);
+    CHECK(bridge_resolve_handle(0xDEAD0001u) == (HANDLE)(uintptr_t)0xDEAD0001u);
+    CHECK(bridge_resolve_handle(0xFE000000u) == (HANDLE)(uintptr_t)0xFE000000u);
+    CHECK(bridge_take_handle(0xDEAD0001u) == NULL);
+    for (i = 0; i < sizeof invalid / sizeof *invalid; ++i) {
+        *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x18000) = invalid[i];
+        CHECK(bridge_read_handle(0x18000) == NULL);
+        CHECK(bridge_resolve_handle(invalid[i]) == NULL && bridge_take_handle(invalid[i]) == NULL);
+    }
+    *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x18000) = 0xBEEF0010u;
+    CHECK(bridge_read_handle(0x18000) == (HANDLE)(uintptr_t)0xBEEF0010u);
+
+    /* Populate exact private bounds without O(N^2) registrations. Exhaustion
+     * must retain the caller's ownership and still deduplicate existing slots.
+     */
+    AcquireSRWLockExclusive(&s_handle_table_lock);
+    for (i = 1; i < BRIDGE_HANDLE_MAX; ++i)
+        bridge_handle_store(i, (HANDLE)((uintptr_t)wide + i * 16));
+    ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&s_handle_table_lock);
+    overflow = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    CHECK(overflow);
+    CHECK(bridge_handle_token(overflow) == 0 && GetHandleInformation(overflow, &flags));
+    CHECK(bridge_handle_token((HANDLE)((uintptr_t)wide + (BRIDGE_HANDLE_MAX - 1) * 16)) ==
+          (BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG | (BRIDGE_HANDLE_MAX - 1)));
+    CHECK(bridge_take_handle(BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG | 1) == (HANDLE)((uintptr_t)wide + 16));
+    CHECK(bridge_handle_token(overflow) == (BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG | 1));
+    CHECK(bridge_take_handle(BRIDGE_HANDLE_TAG | 1) == overflow && CloseHandle(overflow));
+    AcquireSRWLockExclusive(&s_handle_table_lock);
+    for (i = 1; i < BRIDGE_HANDLE_MAX; ++i) bridge_handle_store(i, NULL);
+    ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&s_handle_table_lock);
+
+    shared_handle = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    CHECK(shared_handle);
+    shared_token = bridge_handle_token(shared_handle);
+    same_handle_cohort(0);
+    same_handle_cohort(1);
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(shared_handle));
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+    HANDLE root, threads[WORKERS];
+    wchar_t temporary[MAX_PATH];
+    DWORD count, live_count = 0;
+    unsigned i, round;
+    CHECK(_putenv_s("RECOMP_KERNEL_LOG_BUDGET", "0") == 0);
+    CHECK(_putenv_s("RECOMP_GUEST_LOCK", "0") == 0);
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 16 * 1024 * 1024, MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    CHECK(memory);
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory;
+    InitializeCriticalSection(&barrier.lock);
+    InitializeConditionVariable(&barrier.changed);
+    for (i = 0; i < SERVICES; ++i) *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x10000 + i * 4) = 0x80000000u | ordinals[i];
+    xbox_kernel_set_thunk_address(0x10000, SERVICES);
+    xbox_kernel_bridge_init();
+    for (i = 0; i < SERVICES; ++i) services[i] = guest_word(0x10000 + i * 4);
+    table_edges();
+    CHECK(GetTempPathW(MAX_PATH, temporary));
+    CHECK(GetTempFileNameW(temporary, L"xht", 0, directory));
+    CHECK(DeleteFileW(directory) && CreateDirectoryW(directory, NULL));
+    root = CreateFileW(directory, FILE_LIST_DIRECTORY,
+        FILE_SHARE_READ | FILE_SHARE_WRITE | FILE_SHARE_DELETE, NULL,
+        OPEN_EXISTING, FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS, NULL);
+    CHECK(root != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE);
+    root_token = bridge_handle_token(root);
+    for (i = 0; i < WORKERS; ++i) {
+        threads[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, io_worker, (LPVOID)(uintptr_t)i, 0, NULL);
+        CHECK(threads[i]);
+    }
+    for (round = 0; round < ROUNDS; ++round) {
+        rendezvous();
+        rendezvous();
+        check_live_pairs();
+        CHECK(GetProcessHandleCount(GetCurrentProcess(), &count));
+        if (!round) live_count = count;
+        CHECK(count == live_count);
+        rendezvous();
+    }
+    rendezvous();
+    rendezvous();
+    CHECK(GetProcessHandleCount(GetCurrentProcess(), &count) && count + WORKERS * 2 == live_count);
+    CHECK(WaitForMultipleObjects(WORKERS, threads, TRUE, 10000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    for (i = 0; i < WORKERS; ++i) CHECK(CloseHandle(threads[i]));
+    CHECK(bridge_take_handle(root_token) == root && CloseHandle(root));
+    for (i = 1; i < BRIDGE_HANDLE_MAX; ++i) CHECK(bridge_handle_load(i) == NULL);
+    CHECK(RemoveDirectoryW(directory));
+    DeleteCriticalSection(&barrier.lock);
+    CHECK(VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    puts("PASS: concurrent event/file imports retain unique tokens, exact identities/data and no native-handle leaks");
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_inline_event_callers_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_inline_event_callers_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9cfcae1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_inline_event_callers_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,350 @@
+/* Real event bridges with MM3 XPP's pending-request/wait/cancel contract.
+ * No game assets or guest event opt-in are needed. */
+#include "../../src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c"
+
+#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { fprintf(stderr, "FAIL line %d: %s status=%08X error=%lu\n", __LINE__, #c, g_eax, GetLastError()); fflush(stderr); exit(1); } } while (0)
+#define EVENT_VA 0x22000u
+#define REQUEST_VA 0x30000u
+#define TIMEOUT_VA 0x26000u
+#define SETTER_PC 0x0035C348u
+#define WAIT_PC 0x0035D553u
+#define CANCEL_WAIT_PC 0x0035D56Cu
+#define AUTO_WAIT_PC 0x0035C7F1u
+#define UNRELATED_PC 0x00343D57u
+#define USB_PENDING 0x40000000u
+
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup(uint32_t address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup_manual(uint32_t address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static RECOMP_TLS uint32_t test_stack = 0x28000u;
+static const uint32_t callers[] = { SETTER_PC, WAIT_PC, CANCEL_WAIT_PC, AUTO_WAIT_PC };
+
+static uint32_t invoke(unsigned ordinal, uint32_t caller, const uint32_t *args, unsigned count)
+{
+    unsigned slot = ordinal == 145 ? 0 : ordinal == 159 ? 1 : 2;
+    uint32_t *stack = (uint32_t *)(memory + test_stack);
+    uint32_t saved[6];
+    g_esp = test_stack;
+    g_ecx = 0x12345678u; g_edx = 0x23456789u; g_ebx = REQUEST_VA;
+    g_esi = 0x3456789Au; g_edi = 0x456789ABu; g_ebp = 0x56789ABCu;
+    saved[0] = g_ecx; saved[1] = g_edx; saved[2] = g_ebx;
+    saved[3] = g_esi; saved[4] = g_edi; saved[5] = g_ebp;
+    stack[0] = caller;
+    memcpy(stack + 1, args, count * sizeof(*args));
+    recomp_func_t fn = recomp_lookup_kernel(KERNEL_VA_BASE + slot * 4);
+    CHECK(fn != NULL);
+    fn();
+    CHECK(g_esp == test_stack + 4 + count * 4);
+    CHECK(g_xbox_kernel_caller == caller);
+    CHECK(g_ecx == saved[0] && g_edx == saved[1] && g_ebx == saved[2]);
+    CHECK(g_esi == saved[3] && g_edi == saved[4] && g_ebp == saved[5]);
+    return g_eax;
+}
+
+static uint32_t set_event(uint32_t object, uint32_t caller)
+{
+    uint32_t args[] = { object, 0, 0 };
+    return invoke(145, caller, args, 3);
+}
+
+static uint32_t wait_event(uint32_t object, uint32_t caller, uint32_t timeout)
+{
+    uint32_t args[] = { object, 0, 0, 0, timeout };
+    return invoke(159, caller, args, 5);
+}
+
+static void prepare_event(uint32_t object, unsigned type, unsigned signaled)
+{
+    /* Only Type and Size identify the event; other header bytes are arbitrary
+     * in the real XPP stack-built headers (00048601 / 01040E00). */
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(object) = 0x01040E00u | type;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(object + 4) = signaled;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(object + 8) = object + 8;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(object + 12) = object + 8;
+}
+
+static void prepare_request(uint32_t request, uint32_t event)
+{
+    memset(memory + request, 0, 48);
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(request) = 0x00004030u;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(request + 4) = USB_PENDING;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(request + 8) = 0x0035C33Au;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(request + 12) = event;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(request + 16) = 0x11223344u;
+}
+
+typedef struct {
+    HANDLE start, finished;
+    uint32_t request, event, stack;
+    unsigned delay;
+    volatile LONG damaged, completed;
+} COMPLETION;
+
+static DWORD WINAPI complete_request(void *argument)
+{
+    COMPLETION *c = argument;
+    test_stack = c->stack;
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(c->start, 2000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    if (c->delay) Sleep(c->delay);
+    if (BRIDGE_MEM32(c->request) != 0x4030u ||
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(c->request + 8) != 0x0035C33Au ||
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(c->request + 12) != c->event ||
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(c->request + 16) != 0x11223344u) {
+        InterlockedExchange(&c->damaged, 1);
+    } else {
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(c->request + 4) = 0;
+        CHECK(set_event(c->event, SETTER_PC) == 0);
+        InterlockedExchange(&c->completed, 1);
+    }
+    SetEvent(c->finished);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static HANDLE start_completion(COMPLETION *c, uint32_t request, uint32_t event, unsigned delay, unsigned index)
+{
+    memset(c, 0, sizeof(*c));
+    c->start = CreateEventA(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    c->finished = CreateEventA(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    c->request = request; c->event = event;
+    c->stack = 0x29000u + index * 0x1000u; c->delay = delay;
+    CHECK(c->start && c->finished);
+    HANDLE worker = CreateThread(NULL, 0, complete_request, c, 0, NULL);
+    CHECK(worker != NULL);
+    return worker;
+}
+
+static void finish_completion(COMPLETION *c, HANDLE worker)
+{
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(c->finished, 2000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(worker, 2000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    CloseHandle(worker); CloseHandle(c->start); CloseHandle(c->finished);
+}
+
+static unsigned shadow_count(void)
+{
+    unsigned n = 0;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < KE_SHADOW_SIZE; ++i) n += g_ke_shadow[i].in_use != 0;
+    return n;
+}
+
+static void check_early(void)
+{
+    for (unsigned type = 0; type < 2; ++type) {
+        prepare_event(EVENT_VA, type, 0);
+        prepare_request(REQUEST_VA, EVENT_VA);
+        COMPLETION completion;
+        HANDLE worker = start_completion(&completion, REQUEST_VA, EVENT_VA, 0, 0);
+        SetEvent(completion.start);
+        finish_completion(&completion, worker); /* callback precedes wait/shadow registration */
+        CHECK(completion.completed && !completion.damaged);
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA + 4) == 1);
+        CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, WAIT_PC, TIMEOUT_VA + 8) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA + 4) == (type ? 0u : 1u));
+        CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, AUTO_WAIT_PC, TIMEOUT_VA + 8) == (type ? STATUS_TIMEOUT : STATUS_SUCCESS));
+    }
+}
+
+static void check_late(void)
+{
+    prepare_event(EVENT_VA, 0, 0);
+    prepare_request(REQUEST_VA, EVENT_VA);
+    COMPLETION completion;
+    HANDLE worker = start_completion(&completion, REQUEST_VA, EVENT_VA, 25, 0);
+    SetEvent(completion.start);
+    CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, WAIT_PC, 0) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+    /* A successful wait cannot release the pending stack request early. */
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(REQUEST_VA + 4) == 0);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(REQUEST_VA + 8) == 0x0035C33Au);
+    finish_completion(&completion, worker);
+    CHECK(completion.completed && !completion.damaged);
+}
+
+static void check_cancel(void)
+{
+    prepare_event(EVENT_VA, 1, 0);
+    prepare_request(REQUEST_VA, EVENT_VA);
+    COMPLETION completion;
+    HANDLE worker = start_completion(&completion, REQUEST_VA, EVENT_VA, 0, 0);
+    /* XPP 35D526 uses a 50ms relative wait. Only timeout branches to request
+     * cancellation, followed by the infinite wait at 35D56C. */
+    CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, WAIT_PC, TIMEOUT_VA) == STATUS_TIMEOUT);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(REQUEST_VA + 4) == USB_PENDING);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA + 4) == 0);
+    SetEvent(completion.start); /* cancellation retires the outstanding request */
+    CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, CANCEL_WAIT_PC, 0) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(REQUEST_VA + 4) == 0);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA + 4) == 0);
+    finish_completion(&completion, worker);
+    CHECK(completion.completed && !completion.damaged);
+}
+
+static void check_negative(void)
+{
+    prepare_event(EVENT_VA, 0, 0);
+    prepare_request(REQUEST_VA, EVENT_VA);
+    CHECK(xbox_kernel_set_inline_event_callers(NULL, 0) == 0);
+    COMPLETION completion;
+    HANDLE worker = start_completion(&completion, REQUEST_VA, EVENT_VA, 0, 0);
+    uint32_t status = wait_event(EVENT_VA, WAIT_PC, TIMEOUT_VA);
+    CHECK(status & 0x80000000u); CHECK(status != STATUS_TIMEOUT);
+    CHECK(GetLastError() == ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE);
+    /* Retail XPP regards this non-timeout result as completion. Reusing its
+     * request storage now reproduces the invalid callback seen in the log. */
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(REQUEST_VA + 8) = 0x040172F0u;
+    SetEvent(completion.start);
+    finish_completion(&completion, worker);
+    CHECK(completion.damaged && !completion.completed);
+    CHECK(shadow_count() == 0);
+}
+
+static void check_scope(void)
+{
+    uint32_t configured[4];
+    memcpy(configured, callers, sizeof configured);
+    CHECK(xbox_kernel_set_inline_event_callers(configured, 4) == 0);
+    memset(configured, 0, sizeof configured); /* list was copied */
+    prepare_event(EVENT_VA, 0, 0);
+    CHECK(set_event(EVENT_VA, SETTER_PC) == 0);
+    CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, WAIT_PC, TIMEOUT_VA + 8) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+    unsigned slots = shadow_count();
+    CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, UNRELATED_PC, TIMEOUT_VA + 8) & 0x80000000u);
+    CHECK(GetLastError() == ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE);
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA + 4) = 0;
+    CHECK(set_event(EVENT_VA, UNRELATED_PC) == 0);
+    CHECK(GetLastError() == ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA + 4) == 0 && shadow_count() == slots);
+    /* The title's unrelated D3D notification event remains on its old path. */
+    prepare_event(EVENT_VA + 0x20, 0, 0);
+    CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA + 0x20, UNRELATED_PC, TIMEOUT_VA + 8) & 0x80000000u);
+    CHECK(shadow_count() == slots);
+    CHECK(xbox_kernel_set_inline_event_callers(NULL, 1) == -1);
+    CHECK(xbox_kernel_set_inline_event_callers(callers, 17) == -1);
+    uint32_t bad[] = {0};
+    CHECK(xbox_kernel_set_inline_event_callers(bad, 1) == -1);
+    CHECK(set_event(EVENT_VA, SETTER_PC) == 0);
+    /* Events created by KeInitializeEvent keep their ordinary shadow behavior
+     * even when the caller is outside the inline-event allow-list. */
+    uint32_t args[] = { EVENT_VA, 1, 1 };
+    invoke(108, UNRELATED_PC, args, 3);
+    CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, UNRELATED_PC, TIMEOUT_VA + 8) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+    CHECK(shadow_count() == slots);
+}
+
+static void check_invalid(void)
+{
+    int type = -1;
+    uint32_t invalid[] = { 0, 0x1000, EVENT_VA + 1, 0x50000, 0xFFFFFFFC, 0x80000000 };
+    g_xbox_kernel_caller = WAIT_PC;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof invalid / sizeof invalid[0]; ++i)
+        CHECK(ke_guest_event(invalid[i], &type) == NULL);
+    prepare_event(EVENT_VA, 2, 0);
+    CHECK(ke_guest_event(EVENT_VA, &type) == NULL);
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA) = 0x00080000;
+    CHECK(ke_guest_event(EVENT_VA, &type) == NULL);
+    prepare_event(EVENT_VA, 0, 0);
+    DWORD protection;
+    CHECK(VirtualProtect(memory + EVENT_VA, 0x1000, PAGE_READONLY, &protection));
+    CHECK(ke_guest_event(EVENT_VA, &type) == NULL);
+    CHECK(set_event(EVENT_VA, SETTER_PC) == 0);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA + 4) == 0);
+    CHECK(VirtualProtect(memory + EVENT_VA, 0x1000, protection, &protection));
+    /* A syntactically valid header whose last word has no committed backing. */
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x3FFF4) = 0x00040000;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x3FFF8) = 0;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(0x3FFFC) = 0x3FFFC;
+    g_xbox_kernel_caller = WAIT_PC;
+    CHECK(ke_guest_event(0x3FFF4, &type) == NULL);
+    CHECK(shadow_count() == 0);
+}
+
+static void check_reuse(void)
+{
+    DWORD before, after;
+    CHECK(GetProcessHandleCount(GetCurrentProcess(), &before));
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < KE_SHADOW_SIZE + 64; ++i) {
+        unsigned type = i & 1;
+        prepare_event(EVENT_VA, type, 0);
+        CHECK(set_event(EVENT_VA, SETTER_PC) == 0);
+        CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, WAIT_PC, TIMEOUT_VA + 8) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA + 4) == (type ? 0u : 1u));
+        /* Reinitializing the same type also clears a still-signaled host event. */
+        prepare_event(EVENT_VA, type, 0);
+        CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, AUTO_WAIT_PC, TIMEOUT_VA + 8) == STATUS_TIMEOUT);
+    }
+    CHECK(shadow_count() == 1);
+    CHECK(GetProcessHandleCount(GetCurrentProcess(), &after));
+    CHECK(after == before + 1);
+    ke_shadow_remove(EVENT_VA);
+    CHECK(GetProcessHandleCount(GetCurrentProcess(), &after)); CHECK(after == before);
+}
+
+static void check_capacity(void)
+{
+    DWORD before, after;
+    CHECK(GetProcessHandleCount(GetCurrentProcess(), &before));
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < KE_SHADOW_SIZE; ++i) {
+        HANDLE event = CreateEventA(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+        CHECK(event != NULL); ke_shadow_insert(0x10000u + i * 16, event);
+    }
+    CHECK(shadow_count() == KE_SHADOW_SIZE);
+    prepare_event(EVENT_VA, 0, 0);
+    g_xbox_kernel_caller = WAIT_PC;
+    int type;
+    CHECK(ke_guest_event(EVENT_VA, &type) == NULL);
+    CHECK(wait_event(EVENT_VA, WAIT_PC, TIMEOUT_VA + 8) & 0x80000000u);
+    CHECK(shadow_count() == KE_SHADOW_SIZE && BRIDGE_MEM32(EVENT_VA + 4) == 0);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < KE_SHADOW_SIZE; ++i) ke_shadow_remove(0x10000u + i * 16);
+    CHECK(GetProcessHandleCount(GetCurrentProcess(), &after)); CHECK(after == before);
+}
+
+static void check_concurrent(void)
+{
+    COMPLETION completion[4]; HANDLE worker[4];
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
+        uint32_t event = EVENT_VA + i * 0x20, request = REQUEST_VA + i * 0x40;
+        prepare_event(event, 1, 0); prepare_request(request, event);
+        worker[i] = start_completion(&completion[i], request, event, 0, i);
+    }
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; ++i) SetEvent(completion[i].start);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
+        CHECK(wait_event(completion[i].event, WAIT_PC, 0) == STATUS_SUCCESS);
+        finish_completion(&completion[i], worker[i]);
+        CHECK(completion[i].completed && !completion[i].damaged);
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(completion[i].event + 4) == 0);
+    }
+    CHECK(shadow_count() == 4);
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    CHECK(argc == 2);
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_TITLE_KEVENTS", "0"); _putenv_s("RECOMP_ASYNC_WAIT_TRACE", "0");
+    _putenv_s("MM3_BUILDING_TRACE", "0"); _putenv_s("RECOMP_KERNEL_LOG_BUDGET", "0");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_GUEST_LOCK", "0");
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 0x100000, MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_NOACCESS);
+    CHECK(memory && VirtualAlloc(memory, 0x40000, MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE) == memory);
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory; g_xbox_map_size = 0x100000;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 3; ++i) {
+        unsigned ordinal = i == 0 ? 145 : i == 1 ? 159 : 108;
+        g_slot_ordinals[i] = ordinal; g_slot_bridges[i] = bridge_for_ordinal(ordinal);
+        g_slot_arg_bytes[i] = stdcall_args_for_ordinal(ordinal);
+    }
+    ((LARGE_INTEGER *)(memory + TIMEOUT_VA))->QuadPart = -500000;
+    ((LARGE_INTEGER *)(memory + TIMEOUT_VA + 8))->QuadPart = 0;
+    CHECK(xbox_kernel_set_inline_event_callers(callers, 4) == 0);
+    if (!strcmp(argv[1], "early")) check_early();
+    else if (!strcmp(argv[1], "late")) check_late();
+    else if (!strcmp(argv[1], "cancel")) check_cancel();
+    else if (!strcmp(argv[1], "negative")) check_negative();
+    else if (!strcmp(argv[1], "scope")) check_scope();
+    else if (!strcmp(argv[1], "invalid")) check_invalid();
+    else if (!strcmp(argv[1], "reuse")) check_reuse();
+    else if (!strcmp(argv[1], "capacity")) check_capacity();
+    else if (!strcmp(argv[1], "concurrent")) check_concurrent();
+    else CHECK(0);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < KE_SHADOW_SIZE; ++i)
+        if (g_ke_shadow[i].in_use) ke_shadow_remove(g_ke_shadow[i].guest_va);
+    VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
+    printf("PASS: inline event callers %s; RECOMP_TITLE_KEVENTS=0\n", argv[1]);
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_interrupt_sync_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_interrupt_sync_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ef25812
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_interrupt_sync_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@
+/* Synthetic guest callbacks exercise the production interrupt bridge. */
+#ifndef KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+#define KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE "../../src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c"
+#endif
+#include KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+
+#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "Interrupt synchronization check failed at line %d: %s\n", \
+            __LINE__, #c); \
+    ExitProcess(1); \
+} } while (0)
+
+enum { INTERRUPT = 0x20000, SYNC_ROUTINE = 0x22000, ISR_ROUTINE = 0x24000,
+       SYNC_CONTEXT = 0x26000, VECTOR = 3 };
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static HANDLE worker_started, callback_entered, callback_release;
+static volatile LONG sync_callbacks, isr_callbacks;
+static int exclusion_mode, hold_callback;
+
+static void guest_sync(void)
+{
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) == 0);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) == SYNC_CONTEXT);
+    if (!exclusion_mode) CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 16);
+    InterlockedIncrement(&sync_callbacks);
+    if (hold_callback) {
+        CHECK(SetEvent(callback_entered));
+        CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(callback_release, 3000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    }
+    g_eax = 0xA5;
+    g_esp += 8; /* Guest BOOLEAN callback stdcall ret 4. */
+}
+
+static void guest_isr(void)
+{
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 16);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) == 0);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) == INTERRUPT);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 8) == SYNC_CONTEXT);
+    InterlockedIncrement(&isr_callbacks);
+    g_eax = 1;
+    g_esp += 12; /* Guest ServiceRoutine stdcall ret 8. */
+}
+
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup(uint32_t address)
+{
+    if (address == SYNC_ROUTINE) return guest_sync;
+    if (address == ISR_ROUTINE) return guest_isr;
+    return NULL;
+}
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup_manual(uint32_t address)
+{
+    (void)address;
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+static void call_sync(void)
+{
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) = INTERRUPT;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) = SYNC_ROUTINE;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 8) = SYNC_CONTEXT;
+    uint32_t stack_before = g_esp;
+    bridge_KeSynchronizeExecution();
+    CHECK(g_esp == stack_before && g_eax == 0xA5);
+}
+
+static DWORD WINAPI worker(LPVOID run_isr)
+{
+    g_esp = run_isr ? 0x90000 : 0x80000;
+    g_fs_base = run_isr ? 0x18000 : 0x14000;
+    uint32_t stack_before = g_esp;
+    CHECK(SetEvent(worker_started));
+    if (run_isr) CHECK(kernel_raise_interrupt(VECTOR) == 1);
+    else call_sync();
+    CHECK(g_esp == stack_before);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 0);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static HANDLE start_worker(int run_isr)
+{
+    CHECK(ResetEvent(worker_started));
+    HANDLE thread = CreateThread(NULL, 0, worker,
+                                run_isr ? (LPVOID)1 : NULL, 0, NULL);
+    CHECK(thread);
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(worker_started, 3000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    return thread;
+}
+
+static void join_worker(HANDLE thread)
+{
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(thread, 3000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(thread));
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    exclusion_mode = argc > 1 && !strcmp(argv[1], "exclusion");
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 16 * 1024 * 1024,
+                          MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    CHECK(memory);
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory;
+    g_fs_base = 0x10000;
+    g_esp = 0x30000;
+    worker_started = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    callback_entered = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    callback_release = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    CHECK(worker_started && callback_entered && callback_release);
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(INTERRUPT) = ISR_ROUTINE;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(INTERRUPT + 4) = SYNC_CONTEXT;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(INTERRUPT + 8) = VECTOR;
+    g_connected_isr[VECTOR] = INTERRUPT;
+
+    if (argc > 1 && !strcmp(argv[1], "preemption")) {
+        /* The separate ISR gate must never recreate the audio timeout: a
+         * device interrupt completes while another thread owns DPC level. */
+        int saved_irql = xbox_IrqlEnterInterrupt(2);
+        HANDLE isr_thread = start_worker(1);
+        join_worker(isr_thread);
+        CHECK(isr_callbacks == 1 && sync_callbacks == 0);
+        xbox_IrqlLeaveInterrupt(saved_irql);
+    } else if (exclusion_mode) {
+        /* The ISR owns the processor. A passive synchronization request must
+         * wait before entering its callback or touching the shared SYNC_CONTEXT. */
+        int saved_irql = xbox_IrqlEnterInterrupt(16);
+        HANDLE sync_thread = start_worker(0);
+        CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(sync_thread, 100) == WAIT_TIMEOUT);
+        CHECK(sync_callbacks == 0);
+        xbox_IrqlLeaveInterrupt(saved_irql);
+        join_worker(sync_thread);
+        CHECK(sync_callbacks == 1);
+
+        /* Conversely, a synchronization callback excludes the real ISR
+         * dispatcher until it returns. No interrupt is discarded. */
+        hold_callback = 1;
+        sync_thread = start_worker(0);
+        CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(callback_entered, 3000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+        HANDLE isr_thread = start_worker(1);
+        CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(isr_thread, 100) == WAIT_TIMEOUT);
+        CHECK(isr_callbacks == 0);
+        CHECK(SetEvent(callback_release));
+        join_worker(sync_thread);
+        join_worker(isr_thread);
+        CHECK(sync_callbacks == 2 && isr_callbacks == 1);
+    } else {
+        /* A passive caller and a nested DPC caller both observe ISR IRQL,
+         * keep the callback's return value and restore their prior IRQL. */
+        call_sync();
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 0);
+        int saved_irql = xbox_IrqlEnterInterrupt(2);
+        call_sync();
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 2);
+        xbox_IrqlLeaveInterrupt(saved_irql);
+        CHECK(sync_callbacks == 2);
+
+        BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) = 0; /* Missing routine remains a false result. */
+        bridge_KeSynchronizeExecution();
+        CHECK(g_esp == 0x30000 && g_eax == 0 && sync_callbacks == 2);
+    }
+
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 0);
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(worker_started));
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(callback_entered));
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(callback_release));
+    CHECK(VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    printf("PASS: interrupt synchronization %s; callback arguments, result "
+           "and stack preserved\n", exclusion_mode ? "exclusion" : "IRQL");
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_log_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_log_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..60420ee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_log_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+/* Exercise the real dispatcher across guest threads with no game assets. */
+#include "kernel.h"
+#include "xbox_memory_layout.h"
+#include <io.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+typedef void (*guest_fn)(void);
+extern guest_fn recomp_lookup_kernel(uint32_t);
+extern RECOMP_TLS uint32_t g_eax, g_esp;
+extern ptrdiff_t g_xbox_mem_offset;
+void *recomp_lookup(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+void *recomp_lookup_manual(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static uint32_t service;
+
+static void dispatch(guest_fn fn, uint32_t stack)
+{
+    g_esp = stack;
+    *(uint32_t *)(memory + stack) = 0xBEEF0001;
+    fn();
+    if (g_esp != stack + 4 || g_eax != 0)
+        abort();
+}
+
+static DWORD WINAPI worker(LPVOID stack)
+{
+    guest_fn fn = recomp_lookup_kernel(service);
+    unsigned i;
+    if (!fn)
+        return 1;
+    for (i = 0; i < 10000; ++i)
+        dispatch(fn, (uint32_t)(uintptr_t)stack);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static unsigned occurrences(const char *text, const char *needle)
+{
+    unsigned count = 0;
+    while ((text = strstr(text, needle)) != NULL) {
+        count++;
+        text += strlen(needle);
+    }
+    return count;
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    int summary = argc == 2 && strcmp(argv[1], "summary") == 0;
+    int budget = argc == 2 && strcmp(argv[1], "budget") == 0;
+    FILE *captured;
+    int saved_stderr;
+    HANDLE threads[2];
+    char output[4096];
+    size_t length;
+    unsigned i;
+    guest_fn fn;
+    if (_putenv_s("RECOMP_KERNEL_LOG_BUDGET", budget ? "3" : "0") ||
+        _putenv_s("RECOMP_KERNEL_SUMMARY", summary ? "1" : "") ||
+        _putenv_s("RECOMP_GUEST_LOCK", "0"))
+        return 10;
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 16 * 1024 * 1024,
+                          MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    if (!memory)
+        return 11;
+    g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory;
+    *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x10000) = 0x80000000u | 103;
+    xbox_kernel_set_thunk_address(0x10000, 1);
+    xbox_kernel_bridge_init();
+    service = *(uint32_t *)(memory + 0x10000);
+
+    fflush(stderr);
+    captured = tmpfile();
+    saved_stderr = _dup(_fileno(stderr));
+    if (!captured || saved_stderr < 0 ||
+        _dup2(_fileno(captured), _fileno(stderr)) != 0)
+        return 12;
+    for (i = 0; i < 2; ++i) {
+        threads[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, worker,
+                                  (LPVOID)(uintptr_t)(0x20000 + i * 0x1000), 0, NULL);
+        if (!threads[i])
+            return 13;
+    }
+    if (WaitForMultipleObjects(2, threads, TRUE, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0)
+        return 14;
+    for (i = 0; i < 2; ++i) {
+        DWORD result = 1;
+        GetExitCodeThread(threads[i], &result);
+        CloseHandle(threads[i]);
+        if (result)
+            return 15;
+    }
+    /* Pass the old mandatory-summary threshold, then dispatch once more. */
+    Sleep(2100);
+    fn = recomp_lookup_kernel(service);
+    if (!fn)
+        return 16;
+    dispatch(fn, 0x22000);
+    fflush(stderr);
+    _dup2(saved_stderr, _fileno(stderr));
+    _close(saved_stderr);
+    rewind(captured);
+    length = fread(output, 1, sizeof output - 1, captured);
+    output[length] = '\0';
+    fclose(captured);
+    VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
+
+    if (occurrences(output, "[KERNEL] #") != (budget ? 3u : 0u) ||
+        occurrences(output, "[KERNEL] summary:") != (summary ? 1u : 0u) ||
+        (budget && (occurrences(output, "[KERNEL] #1:") != 1 ||
+                    occurrences(output, "[KERNEL] #2:") != 1 ||
+                    occurrences(output, "[KERNEL] #3:") != 1)) ||
+        (summary && (!strstr(output, "20001 total calls") ||
+                     !strstr(output, "ordinal 103 x20001")))) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: kernel log mode %s:\n%s", argc > 1 ? argv[1] : "quiet", output);
+        return 1;
+    }
+    printf("PASS: kernel log mode %s preserves quiet gameplay and explicit diagnostics\n",
+           argc > 1 ? argv[1] : "quiet");
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_thread_tib_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_thread_tib_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8e366ea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_thread_tib_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+/* Production KPCR/TLS allocation: DPC-active storage must not alias TLS. */
+#include "kernel.h"
+#include "xbox_memory_layout.h"
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#ifndef MEMORY_LAYOUT_SOURCE
+#define MEMORY_LAYOUT_SOURCE "../../src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.c"
+#endif
+#include MEMORY_LAYOUT_SOURCE
+void *recomp_lookup(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+void *recomp_lookup_manual(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { fprintf(stderr, "thread KPCR line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #c); exit(1); } } while (0)
+static uint8_t *bytes(uint32_t va) { return (uint8_t *)((uintptr_t)g_memory_offset + va); }
+static uint32_t *word(uint32_t va) { return (uint32_t *)bytes(va); }
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    uint8_t *arena = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 32 * 1024 * 1024, MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    uint32_t tib, other, block, context, thread_data;
+    unsigned i;
+    CHECK(arena && argc == 2);
+    g_memory_offset = (ptrdiff_t)arena;
+    InitializeCriticalSection(&g_allocator_lock); g_allocator_lock_initialized = 1;
+    g_tls_template_va = 0x10000; g_tls_total = 64;
+    for (i = 0; i < g_tls_total; i++) bytes(g_tls_template_va)[i] = (uint8_t)(0x60 + i);
+    memset(bytes(XBOX_TIB_MAIN), 0xCC, 0x280);
+    *word(XBOX_TIB_MAIN + 0x08) = 0x780000;
+    *word(XBOX_TIB_MAIN + 0x20) = 0x761000;
+    bytes(XBOX_TIB_MAIN)[0x24] = 2; /* creator happens to be in a DPC */
+    *word(XBOX_TIB_MAIN + 0x58) = 1;
+    tib = xbox_AllocThreadTib(); other = xbox_AllocThreadTib();
+    CHECK(tib && other && tib != other);
+    context = *word(tib + 0x28); block = *word(context + 0x28); thread_data = *word(block);
+    CHECK(*word(tib) == 0xFFFFFFFFu && *word(tib + 0x18) == tib);
+    CHECK(*word(tib + 0x04) == block + g_tls_total && *word(tib + 0x08) == 0x780000);
+    CHECK(*word(tib + 0x20) == 0x761000);
+    CHECK(thread_data == block + g_tls_total && context == thread_data + g_tls_thread_size);
+    CHECK(!memcmp(bytes(block + 4), bytes(g_tls_template_va + 4), g_tls_total - 4));
+    CHECK(context != *word(other + 0x28));
+    if (!strcmp(argv[1], "state")) {
+        CHECK(bytes(tib)[0x24] == 0 && *word(tib + 0x58) == 0);
+        CHECK(*word(tib + 0x1C) == tib);
+        CHECK(bytes(XBOX_TIB_MAIN)[0x24] == 2 && *word(XBOX_TIB_MAIN + 0x58) == 1);
+        *word(tib + 0x58) = 1;
+        CHECK(*word(other + 0x58) == 0);
+    } else {
+        uint8_t snapshot[64 + 64 + 0x200];
+        CHECK(sizeof snapshot == g_tls_total + g_tls_thread_size + 0x200);
+        memcpy(snapshot, bytes(block), sizeof snapshot);
+        *word(tib + 0x58) = 1;
+        CHECK(!memcmp(snapshot, bytes(block), sizeof snapshot));
+        *word(tib + 0x58) = 0;
+        CHECK(!memcmp(snapshot, bytes(block), sizeof snapshot));
+        CHECK(block >= tib + 0x280); /* KPCR 0x28 prefix + 0x258 KPRCB. */
+    }
+    xbox_HeapFree(tib); xbox_HeapFree(other);
+    CHECK(VirtualFree(arena, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    printf("PASS thread KPCR %s: independent execution state and nonoverlapping TLS/bootstrap storage\n", argv[1]);
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_timer_lifecycle_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_timer_lifecycle_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f291315
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/kernel_timer_lifecycle_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,122 @@
+/* Timer state must be published before callbacks can rearm or retire it. */
+#define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
+#include <windows.h>
+static int expire_on_reset;
+static LONGLONG system_now = 133000000000000000LL;
+static ULONGLONG tick_now = 100000;
+static LONGLONG audio_deadline;
+static unsigned completed_audio_work;
+static VOID __stdcall test_query_time(PLARGE_INTEGER out) { out->QuadPart = system_now; }
+static ULONGLONG WINAPI test_tick(void) { return tick_now; }
+#define xbox_KeQuerySystemTime test_query_time
+#define GetTickCount64 test_tick
+static void kernel_fire_due_timer(int i, long long now);
+static BOOL WINAPI watched_reset(HANDLE event)
+{
+    if (expire_on_reset) {
+        expire_on_reset = 0;
+        kernel_fire_due_timer(0, 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFLL);
+    }
+    return ResetEvent(event);
+}
+#define ResetEvent watched_reset
+#ifndef KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+#define KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE "../../src/kernel/kernel_bridge.c"
+#endif
+#include KERNEL_BRIDGE_SOURCE
+#undef ResetEvent
+#define CHECK(c) do { if (!(c)) { fprintf(stderr, "timer lifecycle line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #c); ExitProcess(1); } } while (0)
+enum { TIMER = 0x20000, DPC = 0x22000, ROUTINE = 0x26000 };
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static HANDLE timer_event;
+static unsigned callbacks;
+static const char *mode;
+static void guest_dpc(void)
+{
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 2);
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) == DPC);
+    callbacks++;
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "order")) {
+        CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(TIMER + 4) == 1);
+        CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(timer_event, 0) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    } else if (!strcmp(mode, "rearm")) {
+        kernel_set_timer(TIMER, -1000000000LL, 0, DPC);
+        CHECK(!g_eax);
+    } else if (!strcmp(mode, "retire")) {
+        memset(memory + TIMER, 0xA5, 40);
+    } else if (!strcmp(mode, "audio_deadline")) {
+        /* MM3 sub_0027B554 -> sub_0027B389: deferred audio work that is
+         * still in the future rearms KeSetTimer at that absolute time. */
+        if (system_now < audio_deadline) kernel_set_timer(TIMER, audio_deadline, 0, DPC);
+        else completed_audio_work++;
+    }
+    g_esp += 20;
+}
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup(uint32_t address) { return address == ROUTINE ? guest_dpc : NULL; }
+recomp_func_t recomp_lookup_manual(uint32_t address) { (void)address; return NULL; }
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    CHECK(argc == 2); mode = argv[1];
+    memory = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 16 * 1024 * 1024, MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    CHECK(memory); g_xbox_mem_offset = (ptrdiff_t)memory; g_fs_base = 0x10000; g_esp = 0x80000;
+    InitializeCriticalSection(&g_timer_lock); g_timer_started = 1;
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp) = TIMER; BRIDGE_MEM32(g_esp + 4) = 0;
+    bridge_KeInitializeTimerEx(); timer_event = ke_shadow_lookup(TIMER); CHECK(timer_event);
+    BRIDGE_MEM32(DPC + 12) = ROUTINE;
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "audio_deadline")) {
+        unsigned step;
+        audio_deadline = system_now + 20000000;
+        kernel_set_timer(TIMER, audio_deadline, 0, DPC);
+        for (step = 0; step < 200; step++) {
+            tick_now += 10; system_now += 100000;
+            kernel_fire_due_timer(0, (long long)tick_now);
+        }
+        printf("audio timer: callbacks=%u completed=%u over 200 polling ticks\n", callbacks, completed_audio_work);
+        CHECK(callbacks == 1 && completed_audio_work == 1);
+        ke_shadow_remove(TIMER); VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
+        return 0;
+    }
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "absolute") || !strcmp(mode, "expired") || !strcmp(mode, "relative")) {
+        long long due = !strcmp(mode, "absolute") ? system_now + 20000000LL :
+                        !strcmp(mode, "expired") ? system_now - 1 : -15001;
+        long long expected = !strcmp(mode, "absolute") ? 102000 :
+                             !strcmp(mode, "expired") ? 100000 : 100002;
+        kernel_set_timer(TIMER, due, 0, DPC);
+        CHECK(g_timers[0].due_ms == expected);
+        kernel_fire_due_timer(0, expected - 1); CHECK(!callbacks);
+        kernel_fire_due_timer(0, expected); CHECK(callbacks == 1);
+        ke_shadow_remove(TIMER); VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
+        printf("PASS timer %s: deadline honored without repeated early audio DPCs\n", mode);
+        return 0;
+    }
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "publication")) expire_on_reset = 1;
+    kernel_set_timer(TIMER, 0, !strcmp(mode, "periodic") ? 10 : 0,
+                     !strcmp(mode, "publication") ? 0 : DPC);
+    CHECK(!g_eax);
+    if (!strcmp(mode, "publication")) {
+        /* If expiration beat reset, its signal must not disappear. */
+        CHECK(g_timers[0].timer_va == TIMER || WaitForSingleObject(timer_event, 0) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    } else {
+        long long now = g_timers[0].due_ms;
+        kernel_fire_due_timer(0, now);
+        CHECK(callbacks == 1 && g_esp == 0x80000);
+        if (!strcmp(mode, "rearm")) {
+            CHECK(g_timers[0].timer_va == TIMER && g_timers[0].due_ms > now);
+            CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM32(TIMER + 4) == 0 && WaitForSingleObject(timer_event, 0) == WAIT_TIMEOUT);
+            kernel_fire_due_timer(0, now); CHECK(callbacks == 1);
+            kernel_fire_due_timer(0, g_timers[0].due_ms); CHECK(callbacks == 2);
+        } else if (!strcmp(mode, "retire")) {
+            unsigned i; for (i = 0; i < 40; i++) CHECK(memory[TIMER + i] == 0xA5);
+        } else if (!strcmp(mode, "periodic")) {
+            CHECK(g_timers[0].timer_va == TIMER && g_timers[0].due_ms == now + 10);
+            kernel_fire_due_timer(0, now + 9); CHECK(callbacks == 1);
+            kernel_fire_due_timer(0, now + 10); CHECK(callbacks == 2);
+            CHECK(xbox_kernel_cancel_timer(TIMER));
+            kernel_fire_due_timer(0, now + 100); CHECK(callbacks == 2);
+        } else { CHECK(!g_timers[0].timer_va); }
+    }
+    CHECK(BRIDGE_MEM8(g_fs_base + 0x24) == 0);
+    ke_shadow_remove(TIMER); VirtualFree(memory, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
+    printf("PASS timer %s: state/event ordering, callback lifetime and scheduling\n", mode);
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_command_fence_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_command_fence_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c57fdd2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_command_fence_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,274 @@
+/* Exercise real executor dispatch and the production completion publisher.
+ * Only guest arena setup and GPU readback readiness are supplied by the test. */
+#include "kernel.h"
+#include "xbox_memory_layout.h"
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+
+static int readback_busy;
+static unsigned readback_polls;
+static int fail_next_malloc;
+static void *test_malloc(size_t bytes)
+{
+    if (fail_next_malloc) { fail_next_malloc = 0; return NULL; }
+    return malloc(bytes);
+}
+static int test_writeback_busy(void)
+{
+    ++readback_polls;
+    return readback_busy;
+}
+#define nv2a_d3d_writeback_busy test_writeback_busy
+#define malloc test_malloc
+#include "../../src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.c"
+#undef malloc
+#undef nv2a_d3d_writeback_busy
+
+void *recomp_lookup(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+void *recomp_lookup_manual(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+extern void nv2a_pb_exec_method(uint32_t, uint32_t, uint32_t);
+
+#define CHECK(expr) do { if (!(expr)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #expr); exit(1); \
+} } while (0)
+
+static volatile uint32_t *guest(uint32_t va)
+{
+    return (volatile uint32_t *)((uintptr_t)va + g_memory_offset);
+}
+static void method(uint32_t address, uint32_t value)
+{
+    nv2a_pb_exec_method(0, address, value);
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+    uint8_t *arena = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 0x100000, MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT,
+                                  PAGE_READWRITE);
+    uint8_t *registers = calloc(1, 0x1000000);
+    volatile uint32_t *regs = (volatile uint32_t *)registers;
+    volatile uint32_t *get = (volatile uint32_t *)(registers + NV2A_USER_DMA_GET);
+    volatile uint32_t *put = (volatile uint32_t *)(registers + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT);
+    LONG generation;
+    unsigned polls;
+    XBOX_NV2A_CAPTURE_STATE snapshot;
+    CHECK(arena && registers);
+    g_memory_base = arena;
+    g_memory_size = 0x100000;
+    g_memory_offset = (ptrdiff_t)arena;
+    xbox_nv2a_wake_init(&g_nv2a_wake);
+    *guest(0x10000) = 0x20000;
+    *guest(0x20030) = 0x30000;
+    *guest(0x2002C) = 99; /* The next submitted counter is not completed work. */
+    *guest(0x30000) = 23;
+    *get = 111; *put = 999;
+    CHECK(xbox_Nv2aCommandFence(0x10000, 0xC, 0) == -1);
+    CHECK(xbox_Nv2aMirrorFence(0x10000, 0x2C, 0x30) == 0);
+    CHECK(xbox_Nv2aCommandFence(0x10000, 0xC, 0) == 0);
+
+    /* Startup/idle cannot invent a first release, even before DMA_PUT moves. */
+    generation = xbox_nv2a_wake_snapshot(&g_nv2a_wake);
+    fence_mirrors_tick(0); fence_mirrors_tick(1);
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 23 && *get == 111 && !readback_polls);
+    CHECK(xbox_nv2a_wake_snapshot(&g_nv2a_wake) == generation);
+
+    /* Actual dispatch filters the configured DMA, offset and 3D subchannel. */
+    method(0x01A8, 0xD); method(0x1D6C, 0); method(0x1D70, 100);
+    nv2a_pb_exec_method(1, 0x01A8, 0xC);
+    method(0x1D70, 101);
+    method(0x01A8, 0xC); method(0x1D6C, 4); method(0x1D70, 102);
+    nv2a_pb_exec_method(1, 0x1D6C, 0);
+    method(0x1D70, 103);
+    CHECK(!command_fences_pending());
+    method(0x1D6C, 0);
+    nv2a_pb_exec_method(1, 0x1D70, 104);
+    CHECK(!command_fences_pending());
+
+    /* Zero is a real release; a busy prior readback defers its publication. */
+    readback_busy = 1;
+    method(0x1D70, 0);
+    CHECK(command_fences_pending());
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    *guest(0x2002C) = 12345;
+    fence_mirrors_tick(0); fence_mirrors_tick(1);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 23 && *get == 111);
+    CHECK(xbox_nv2a_wake_snapshot(&g_nv2a_wake) == generation);
+    readback_busy = 0;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 0 && *guest(0x2002C) == 12345 && *get == 111);
+    CHECK(!command_fences_pending());
+    CHECK(xbox_nv2a_wake_snapshot(&g_nv2a_wake) == generation + 1);
+    polls = readback_polls;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(readback_polls == polls); /* No work adds no driver polls. */
+
+    /* Latest execution order wins across wrap, never a numeric MAX. */
+    *guest(0x30000) = 1;
+    method(0x1D70, UINT32_MAX); method(0x1D70, 0);
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 0);
+    method(0x1D70, UINT32_MAX - 1); method(0x1D70, 1);
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 1);
+    method(0x1D70, 3); method(0x1D70, 5);
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 5);
+
+    /* Retain the target at execution, not a later device/get-pointer chain. */
+    *guest(0x22030) = 0x31000;
+    *guest(0x31000) = 0xDEADBEEF;
+    readback_busy = 1;
+    method(0x1D70, 7);
+    *guest(0x10000) = 0x22000;
+    *guest(0x20030) = 0x31000;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 5 && *guest(0x31000) == 0xDEADBEEF);
+    readback_busy = 0;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 7 && *guest(0x31000) == 0xDEADBEEF);
+    method(0x1D70, 9);
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x31000) == 9);
+
+    /* Multiple targets before one readback completion must all be retained.
+     * Returning to the first target is a new ordered write, not a reorder. */
+    readback_busy = 1;
+    method(0x1D70, 10);
+    CHECK(xbox_Nv2aCommandFence(0x10000, 0xC, 0) == -1);
+    *guest(0x22030) = 0x30000;
+    method(0x1D70, 11);
+    *guest(0x22030) = 0x31000;
+    method(0x1D70, 12);
+    method(0x1D70, 14); /* Consecutive writes coalesce only at the tail. */
+    CHECK(g_fence_mirrors[0].command_head && g_fence_mirrors[0].command_tail);
+    CHECK(g_fence_mirrors[0].command_head->target == 0x30000);
+    CHECK(g_fence_mirrors[0].command_tail->target == 0x31000);
+    CHECK(g_fence_mirrors[0].command_tail->value == 14);
+    xbox_Nv2aCaptureSnapshot(&snapshot);
+    CHECK(snapshot.version == 1 && snapshot.bytes == sizeof snapshot);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirrors[0].command_queue_count == 3);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirrors[0].device_bytes == XBOX_NV2A_CAPTURE_DEVICE_BYTES);
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 7 && *guest(0x31000) == 9);
+    readback_busy = 0;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x30000) == 11 && *guest(0x31000) == 14);
+    CHECK(!g_fence_mirrors[0].command_head && !g_fence_mirrors[0].command_tail);
+
+    /* A target-change CRT allocation failure uses the native heap without
+     * publishing any fence/GET/notification or polling prior GPU work. */
+    method(0x1D70, 18);
+    *guest(0x22030) = 0x30000;
+    fail_next_malloc = 1;
+    polls = readback_polls;
+    generation = xbox_nv2a_wake_snapshot(&g_nv2a_wake);
+    method(0x1D70, 20);
+    CHECK(!fail_next_malloc && g_fence_mirrors[0].command_tail->native_heap);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x31000) == 14 && *guest(0x30000) == 11 && *get == 111);
+    CHECK(readback_polls == polls && !g_notify_count &&
+          xbox_nv2a_wake_snapshot(&g_nv2a_wake) == generation);
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x31000) == 18 && *guest(0x30000) == 20 && *get == 111);
+    *guest(0x22030) = 0x31000;
+    *guest(0x31000) = 9;
+
+    /* Unreadable chains cannot change guest bytes or invent pending work. */
+    *guest(0x10000) = 0;
+    method(0x1D70, 11);
+    *guest(0x10000) = 0xFFFFFFF0;
+    method(0x1D70, 11);
+    *guest(0x10000) = 0x22000;
+    *guest(0x22030) = 0;
+    method(0x1D70, 11);
+    CHECK(!command_fences_pending() && *guest(0x31000) == 9);
+    *guest(0x22030) = 0x31000;
+
+    /* A cap retains even an executed fence. Publishing it alongside an old
+     * GET could let guest reserve logic reuse the unread part of that lap. */
+    s_scan_incomplete = 1;
+    readback_busy = 1;
+    method(0x1D70, 13);
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x31000) == 9 && *get == 111);
+    readback_busy = 0;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x31000) == 9 && *get == 111 && s_scan_incomplete);
+    s_get_held = 1; s_get_held_value = 222;
+    readback_busy = 1;
+    method(0x1D70, 15);
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(s_get_held && *get == 111 && *guest(0x31000) == 9);
+    readback_busy = 0;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(!s_get_held && *get == 222 && *put == 999 && s_scan_incomplete);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x31000) == 9 && command_fences_pending());
+    s_scan_incomplete = 0;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x31000) == 15 && !command_fences_pending());
+
+    /* Publication failure retains the exact target/value for a later retry. */
+    method(0x1D70, 17);
+    g_memory_size = 0x29000;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(command_fences_pending() && *guest(0x31000) == 15);
+    g_memory_size = 0x100000;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(regs);
+    CHECK(!command_fences_pending() && *guest(0x31000) == 17);
+
+    /* Other titles retain the original generic counter-snapshot behavior. */
+    *guest(0x12000) = 0x24000;
+    *guest(0x24030) = 0x34000;
+    *guest(0x2402C) = 76;
+    *guest(0x34000) = 55;
+    CHECK(xbox_Nv2aMirrorFence(0x12000, 0x2C, 0x30) == 0);
+    fence_mirrors_tick(0);
+    *guest(0x2402C) = 77;
+    fence_mirrors_tick(1);
+    CHECK(*guest(0x34000) == 76 && *guest(0x31000) == 17);
+
+    /* Diagnostics distinguish the real aperture from a guest software
+     * channel, retain raw device fields, and never query/read back the GPU. */
+    g_nv2a_memory = registers;
+    *guest(0x22008) = 0x2000;
+    *guest(0x237C0) = 0x14000;
+    *guest(0x14040) = 0x4444; *guest(0x14044) = 0x5555;
+    *guest(0x224F8) = XBOX_NV2A_BASE;
+    *(uint32_t *)(registers + NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_SUBROUTINE) = 0x7777;
+    CHECK(xbox_Nv2aNotifyEvent(0x10000, 0x196C, 5) == 0);
+    g_notify_count = 7;
+    s_scan_incomplete = 1;
+    polls = readback_polls;
+    SetLastError(0x12345678);
+    xbox_Nv2aCaptureSnapshot(&snapshot);
+    CHECK(GetLastError() == 0x12345678 && readback_polls == polls);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mmio_valid && snapshot.user_put == 999 && snapshot.user_get == 222);
+    CHECK(snapshot.scan_incomplete == 1 && !snapshot.get_held);
+    CHECK(snapshot.notify_count == 7 && snapshot.notify_param == 5);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirror_count == 2 && !snapshot.counter_mirrors && !snapshot.frame_counters);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirrors[0].device_ptr_va == 0x10000 && snapshot.mirrors[0].device_va == 0x22000);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirrors[0].channel_valid && snapshot.mirrors[0].channel_va == 0x14000);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirrors[0].channel_put == 0x4444 && snapshot.mirrors[0].channel_get == 0x5555);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirrors[0].pfifo_valid && snapshot.mirrors[0].pfifo_subroutine == 0x7777);
+    CHECK(*(uint32_t *)(snapshot.mirrors[0].device + 8) == 0x2000);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirrors[0].fence_valid && snapshot.mirrors[0].fence_value == 17);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirrors[0].command_mode && !snapshot.mirrors[0].command_queue_count);
+    *guest(0x237C0) = XBOX_NV2A_BASE + 0x800000;
+    xbox_Nv2aCaptureSnapshot(&snapshot);
+    CHECK(snapshot.mirrors[0].channel_valid && snapshot.mirrors[0].channel_put == 999 &&
+          snapshot.mirrors[0].channel_get == 222);
+    g_nv2a_memory = NULL;
+    *guest(0x10000) = UINT32_MAX - 8;
+    xbox_Nv2aCaptureSnapshot(&snapshot);
+    CHECK(!snapshot.mmio_valid && !snapshot.mirrors[0].device_valid &&
+          !snapshot.mirrors[0].device_bytes);
+    xbox_Nv2aCaptureSnapshot(NULL);
+
+    puts("PASS: real semaphore dispatch, no idle early fence, readback/cap/GET "
+         "ordering, uint32 wrap, captured targets, generic fallback and read-only state capture");
+    g_memory_base = NULL;
+    free(registers);
+    CHECK(VirtualFree(arena, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_dma_sync_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_dma_sync_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f49c566
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_dma_sync_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,263 @@
+/* Real publication/completion code, with only GPU readiness supplied here. */
+#include "kernel.h"
+#include "xbox_memory_layout.h"
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+
+static int readback_busy;
+static int test_writeback_busy(void) { return readback_busy; }
+#define nv2a_d3d_writeback_busy test_writeback_busy
+#include "../../src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.c"
+#undef nv2a_d3d_writeback_busy
+
+void *recomp_lookup(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+void *recomp_lookup_manual(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+
+#define CHECK(x) do { if (!(x)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #x); ExitProcess(1); \
+} } while (0)
+
+static volatile uint32_t *registers;
+#define REG(offset) (*(volatile uint32_t *)((char *)registers + (offset)))
+static HANDLE waiting;
+static volatile LONG wait_calls, wrong_wait, missed_wake;
+static int inject_completion;
+static BOOL (WINAPI *native_wait)(volatile VOID *, PVOID, SIZE_T, DWORD);
+static VOID (WINAPI *native_wake)(PVOID);
+static uint32_t observed_sequence, observed_get;
+static unsigned observed_completions;
+
+static VOID WINAPI ordered_wake(PVOID address)
+{
+    if (observed_sequence && (uint32_t)g_notify_count == observed_sequence) {
+        CHECK(REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_GET) == observed_get);
+        CHECK(REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_GET) == observed_get);
+        ++observed_completions;
+    }
+    native_wake(address);
+}
+
+static BOOL WINAPI observed_wait(volatile VOID *address, PVOID compare,
+                                 SIZE_T size, DWORD timeout)
+{
+    if (size != sizeof(LONG) || timeout != 1) InterlockedExchange(&wrong_wait, 1);
+    InterlockedIncrement(&wait_calls);
+    SetEvent(waiting);
+    if (inject_completion) {
+        inject_completion = 0;
+        nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_PUT), s_notify_executed);
+        /* Completion occurs after the final predicate but before registration.
+         * Waiting on the old generation must return immediately. */
+        if (!native_wait(address, compare, size, timeout))
+            InterlockedExchange(&missed_wake, 1);
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+    return native_wait(address, compare, size, timeout);
+}
+
+static DWORD WINAPI waiter(LPVOID ignored)
+{
+    (void)ignored;
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaWait(XBOX_NV2A_BASE);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static HANDLE start_wait(void)
+{
+    ResetEvent(waiting);
+    HANDLE thread = CreateThread(NULL, 0, waiter, NULL, 0, NULL);
+    CHECK(thread && WaitForSingleObject(waiting, 5000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    return thread;
+}
+
+static void finish_wait(HANDLE thread)
+{
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(thread, 5000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(thread));
+}
+
+static void test_waits(void)
+{
+    HANDLE thread;
+    unsigned before;
+    native_wait = g_nv2a_wake.wait_address;
+    CHECK(native_wait && g_nv2a_wake.wake_all);
+    g_nv2a_wake.wait_address = observed_wait;
+    waiting = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    CHECK(waiting);
+    g_nv2a_ack_thread = (HANDLE)(uintptr_t)1; /* API checks ownership, not handle use. */
+
+    before = wait_calls;
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaWait(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + 4); /* Unknown base keeps guest polling. */
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaWait(XBOX_NV2A_BASE);     /* Already idle requires no host wait. */
+    CHECK(wait_calls == before);
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, 0x12000);
+    inject_completion = 1;
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaWait(XBOX_NV2A_BASE);
+    CHECK(wait_calls == before + 1 && !missed_wake && !wrong_wait);
+
+    /* A generation-only wake and an older completed boundary cannot report
+     * idle when the producer has published a newer PUT. */
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, 0x13000);
+    thread = start_wait();
+    xbox_nv2a_wake_publish(&g_nv2a_wake);
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(thread, 0) == WAIT_TIMEOUT);
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, 0x14000);
+    nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, 0x13000, s_notify_executed);
+    CHECK(REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS) && WaitForSingleObject(thread, 0) == WAIT_TIMEOUT);
+    nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, 0x14000, s_notify_executed);
+    finish_wait(thread);
+
+    /* Even equal pointers are not idle while the original status register is
+     * nonzero. A raw guest status write has no notification; timeout notices it. */
+    REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS) = 0x80;
+    thread = start_wait();
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(thread, 0) == WAIT_TIMEOUT);
+    REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS) = 0;
+    finish_wait(thread);
+
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, 0x15000);
+    thread = start_wait();
+    InterlockedExchange(&g_nv2a_ack_stop, 1);
+    xbox_nv2a_wake_publish(&g_nv2a_wake);
+    finish_wait(thread);
+    CHECK(REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_GET) == 0x14000 && REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS));
+    g_nv2a_ack_stop = 0;
+
+    /* Native API unavailable retains the yield path and exact predicate. */
+    g_nv2a_wake.wait_address = NULL;
+    thread = CreateThread(NULL, 0, waiter, NULL, 0, NULL);
+    CHECK(thread && WaitForSingleObject(thread, 0) == WAIT_TIMEOUT);
+    nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, 0x15000, s_notify_executed);
+    finish_wait(thread);
+    g_nv2a_wake.wait_address = native_wait;
+    g_nv2a_ack_thread = NULL;
+    CHECK(CloseHandle(waiting));
+}
+
+static void test_notifications(void)
+{
+    LONG generation;
+    native_wake = g_nv2a_wake.wake_all;
+    g_nv2a_wake.wake_all = ordered_wake;
+    CHECK(xbox_Nv2aNotifyEvent(0x10000, 0x196C, 5) == 0);
+    generation = xbox_nv2a_wake_snapshot(&g_nv2a_wake);
+    xbox_Nv2aNop(0); xbox_Nv2aNop(4);
+    CHECK(!s_notify_executed && !g_notify_count);
+    xbox_Nv2aNop(5); xbox_Nv2aNop(5);
+    CHECK(s_notify_executed == 2 && !g_notify_count);
+    CHECK(xbox_nv2a_wake_snapshot(&g_nv2a_wake) == generation);
+    s_scan_incomplete = 1;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(registers);
+    CHECK(!g_notify_count); /* Cap/idle cannot expose an executed NOP. */
+
+    /* A held older checkpoint captures its sequence before a newer partial
+     * submission executes another NOP. Releasing the old readback publishes
+     * only the old sequence, after the old GET, even with a newer live PUT. */
+    s_get_held = 1; s_get_held_value = 0x16000;
+    s_get_held_notify = s_notify_executed;
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, 0x17000);
+    xbox_Nv2aNop(5);
+    readback_busy = 1;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(registers);
+    CHECK(!g_notify_count && REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_GET) == 0x15000);
+    readback_busy = 0;
+    observed_sequence = 2; observed_get = 0x16000;
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(registers);
+    CHECK(g_notify_count == 2 && s_notify_executed == 3 && !s_get_held);
+    CHECK(REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_GET) == 0x16000 && REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_GET) == 0x16000);
+    CHECK(REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT) == 0x17000 && REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS));
+    nv2a_publish_readback_complete(registers);
+    CHECK(g_notify_count == 2); /* Newer capped NOP remains pending. */
+    CHECK(observed_completions);
+    observed_sequence = 3; observed_get = 0x17000;
+    nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, 0x17000, s_notify_executed);
+    CHECK(g_notify_count == 3 && !REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS));
+    s_scan_incomplete = 0;
+
+    /* Notification count is an exact unsigned event sequence across wrap. */
+    s_notify_executed = UINT32_MAX;
+    g_notify_count = -1;
+    xbox_Nv2aNop(5);
+    CHECK(s_notify_executed == 0 && g_notify_count == -1);
+    nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, 0x17000, s_notify_executed);
+    CHECK(g_notify_count == 0);
+    observed_sequence = 0;
+    g_nv2a_wake.wake_all = native_wake;
+}
+
+static volatile LONG producer_ready, producer_done;
+static DWORD WINAPI producer(LPVOID ignored)
+{
+    (void)ignored;
+    for (uint32_t i = 1; i <= 20000; ++i) {
+        xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, i);
+        InterlockedExchange(&producer_ready, (LONG)i);
+        while (InterlockedCompareExchange(&producer_done, 0, 0) != (LONG)i)
+            YieldProcessor();
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static void test_concurrent_stores(void)
+{
+    HANDLE thread = CreateThread(NULL, 0, producer, NULL, 0, NULL);
+    CHECK(thread);
+    for (LONG i = 1; i <= 20000; ++i) {
+        while (InterlockedCompareExchange(&producer_ready, 0, 0) != i)
+            YieldProcessor();
+        nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, (uint32_t)i, s_notify_executed);
+        InterlockedExchange(&producer_done, i);
+        AcquireSRWLockExclusive(&g_nv2a_dma_lock);
+        CHECK(REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT) == REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_PUT));
+        CHECK(REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_GET) == REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_GET));
+        CHECK(REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS) ==
+            (REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_PUT) != REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_GET)));
+        ReleaseSRWLockExclusive(&g_nv2a_dma_lock);
+    }
+    finish_wait(thread);
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+    uint8_t *arena = VirtualAlloc(NULL, 0x100000, MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    uint8_t *mmio = calloc(1, XBOX_NV2A_SIZE);
+    CHECK(arena && mmio);
+    g_memory_base = arena; g_memory_size = 0x100000;
+    g_memory_offset = (ptrdiff_t)arena; g_nv2a_memory = mmio;
+    registers = (volatile uint32_t *)mmio;
+    xbox_nv2a_wake_init(&g_nv2a_wake);
+
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(0x14040, 0x12345678);
+    CHECK(*(uint32_t *)(arena + 0x14040) == 0x12345678 && !g_nv2a_dma_sync);
+    CHECK(!REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_PUT) && !REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_GET));
+    REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_GET) = 0x11000;
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, 0x12000);
+    CHECK(g_nv2a_dma_sync && REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_GET) == 0x11000);
+    CHECK(REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT) == 0x12000 && REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_PUT) == 0x12000);
+    CHECK(REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS));
+    nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, 0x12000, 0);
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, 0x12000);
+    CHECK(!REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS)); /* Same completed PUT is already idle. */
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(0x14040, 0x87654321);
+    CHECK(*(uint32_t *)(arena + 0x14040) == 0x87654321 &&
+          REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT) == 0x12000 && !REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS));
+
+    /* Neither register payload nor completion order is a numeric maximum. */
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, UINT32_MAX - 3);
+    xbox_Nv2aDmaPublish(XBOX_NV2A_BASE + NV2A_USER_DMA_PUT, 0x4000);
+    nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, UINT32_MAX - 3, 0);
+    CHECK(REG(NV2A_PFIFO_DMA_GET) == UINT32_MAX - 3 && REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS));
+    nv2a_publish_consumed(registers, 0x4000, 0);
+    CHECK(REG(NV2A_USER_DMA_GET) == 0x4000 && !REG(NV2A_PGRAPH_STATUS));
+
+    test_waits();
+    test_notifications();
+    test_concurrent_stores();
+    CHECK(!wrong_wait && !missed_wake);
+    puts("PASS: exact DMA publication/consumption, software fallback, busy/wrap ordering, "
+         "concurrent stores, native wait races and deferred NOP/readback checkpoints");
+    g_nv2a_memory = NULL; g_memory_base = NULL;
+    free(mmio); CHECK(VirtualFree(arena, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_fence_wait_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_fence_wait_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0adeef9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_fence_wait_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+/* Direct fence waits keep the original unsigned distance predicate. */
+#include "kernel/nv2a_notify_wait.h"
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+typedef struct {
+    XBOX_NV2A_WAKE wake;
+    volatile uint32_t completed;
+    volatile LONG stop, wait_calls;
+    HANDLE started, waiting;
+    int inject;
+} FIXTURE;
+static FIXTURE *active;
+static BOOL (WINAPI *native_wait)(volatile VOID *, PVOID, SIZE_T, DWORD);
+static volatile LONG bad_timeout, missed_wake;
+
+static BOOL WINAPI measured_wait(volatile VOID *address, PVOID compare,
+                                 SIZE_T size, DWORD timeout)
+{
+    FIXTURE *f = active;
+    if (size != sizeof(LONG) || timeout != 1) InterlockedExchange(&bad_timeout, 1);
+    InterlockedIncrement(&f->wait_calls);
+    SetEvent(f->waiting);
+    if (f->inject) {
+        f->inject = 0;
+        f->completed = 1;
+        xbox_nv2a_wake_publish(&f->wake);
+        if (!native_wait(address, compare, size, timeout))
+            InterlockedExchange(&missed_wake, 1);
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+    return native_wait(address, compare, size, timeout);
+}
+
+static int initialize(FIXTURE *f)
+{
+    memset(f, 0, sizeof *f);
+    f->completed = 0xFFFFFFFEu;
+    xbox_nv2a_wake_init(&f->wake);
+    if (!f->wake.wait_address || !f->wake.wake_all) return 0;
+    native_wait = f->wake.wait_address;
+    f->wake.wait_address = measured_wait;
+    f->started = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    f->waiting = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    active = f;
+    return f->started && f->waiting;
+}
+
+static void cleanup(FIXTURE *f)
+{
+    CloseHandle(f->started);
+    CloseHandle(f->waiting);
+}
+
+static DWORD WINAPI worker(LPVOID parameter)
+{
+    FIXTURE *f = parameter;
+    SetEvent(f->started);
+    xbox_nv2a_fence_wait(&f->wake, &f->completed, 3, 2, &f->stop);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static int concurrent_completion(unsigned kind)
+{
+    FIXTURE f;
+    HANDLE thread;
+    if (!initialize(&f)) return 0;
+    if (kind == 3) {
+        f.wake.wait_address = NULL;
+        f.wake.wake_all = NULL;
+    }
+    thread = CreateThread(NULL, 0, worker, &f, 0, NULL);
+    if (!thread) ExitProcess(20);
+    if (WaitForSingleObject(kind == 3 ? f.started : f.waiting, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0)
+        ExitProcess(21);
+    xbox_nv2a_wake_publish(&f.wake); /* Wake cannot change completion rules. */
+    if (WaitForSingleObject(thread, 0) != WAIT_TIMEOUT) ExitProcess(22);
+    if (kind == 1) InterlockedExchange(&f.stop, 1);
+    else f.completed = 1;
+    if (kind != 2) xbox_nv2a_wake_publish(&f.wake);
+    if (WaitForSingleObject(thread, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0) ExitProcess(23);
+    CloseHandle(thread);
+    if (kind == 1 && f.completed != 0xFFFFFFFEu) ExitProcess(24);
+    cleanup(&f);
+    return !bad_timeout && !missed_wake;
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+    static const struct { uint32_t submitted, completed, limit; int pending; } cases[] = {
+        { 0x1234, 0x1200, 0x20, 1 }, { 0x1234, 0x1214, 0x20, 0 },
+        { 0x1234, 0x1215, 0x20, 0 }, { 3, 0xFFFFFFFEu, 2, 1 },
+        { 3, 1, 2, 0 }, { 3, 2, 2, 0 }, { 3, 3, 2, 0 },
+        { 0xFFFFFFFEu, 1, 2, 1 }, { 0xFFFFFFFEu, 0xFFFFFFFCu, 2, 0 },
+        { 3, 2, 0, 1 }, { 3, 3, 0, 0 }, { 3, 4, 0, 1 },
+        { 3, 4, 0xFFFFFFFFu, 0 }, { 3, 0xFFFFFFFEu, 0xFFFFFFFFu, 0 }
+    };
+    FIXTURE f;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof cases / sizeof cases[0]; i++) {
+        volatile uint32_t completed = cases[i].completed;
+        if (xbox_nv2a_fence_pending(&completed, cases[i].submitted, cases[i].limit)
+                != cases[i].pending || completed != cases[i].completed)
+            return 1;
+    }
+    if (!initialize(&f)) return 2;
+    f.completed = 1;
+    xbox_nv2a_fence_wait(&f.wake, &f.completed, 3, 2, &f.stop);
+    if (f.wait_calls || f.completed != 1) return 3;
+    cleanup(&f);
+    if (!initialize(&f)) return 4;
+    f.inject = 1;
+    xbox_nv2a_fence_wait(&f.wake, &f.completed, 3, 2, &f.stop);
+    if (f.wait_calls != 1 || f.completed != 1 || missed_wake || bad_timeout) return 5;
+    cleanup(&f);
+    for (unsigned kind = 0; kind < 4; kind++)
+        if (!concurrent_completion(kind)) return 6 + kind;
+    puts("PASS: exact unsigned fence distances, wrap boundaries, early completion, "
+         "check-to-wait race, spurious/stop wakes and bounded fallback");
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_notify_wait_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_notify_wait_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2f5a9a8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_notify_wait_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@
+/* Exercise the exact host wait helper without GPU devices or game assets. */
+#include "kernel/nv2a_notify_wait.h"
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+typedef struct {
+    XBOX_NV2A_WAKE wake;
+    volatile uint32_t get, put;
+    volatile LONG notifications, stop, ready_count, wait_calls;
+    HANDLE started, waiting;
+    int inject_completion;
+} FIXTURE;
+static FIXTURE *active_fixture;
+static BOOL (WINAPI *real_wait)(volatile VOID *, PVOID, SIZE_T, DWORD);
+static __declspec(thread) int t_wait_reported;
+static volatile LONG bad_timeout, missed_wake;
+
+static BOOL WINAPI observed_wait(volatile VOID *address, PVOID observed,
+                                 SIZE_T size, DWORD timeout)
+{
+    FIXTURE *f = active_fixture;
+    if (size != sizeof(LONG) || timeout != 1) InterlockedExchange(&bad_timeout, 1);
+    InterlockedIncrement(&f->wait_calls);
+    if (!t_wait_reported) {
+        t_wait_reported = 1;
+        InterlockedIncrement(&f->ready_count);
+        SetEvent(f->waiting);
+    }
+    /* This hook is entered AFTER the helper's second predicate check but
+     * BEFORE the native atomic wait. Its wake happens before any waiter can
+     * be registered, so an event-only implementation would lose it. */
+    if (f->inject_completion) {
+        f->inject_completion = 0;
+        f->get = f->put;
+        xbox_nv2a_wake_publish(&f->wake);
+        if (!real_wait(address, observed, size, timeout))
+            InterlockedExchange(&missed_wake, 1);
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+    return real_wait(address, observed, size, timeout);
+}
+
+static int init_fixture(FIXTURE *f)
+{
+    memset(f, 0, sizeof *f);
+    xbox_nv2a_wake_init(&f->wake);
+    if (!f->wake.wait_address || !f->wake.wake_all) return 0;
+    real_wait = f->wake.wait_address;
+    f->wake.wait_address = observed_wait;
+    f->put = 1;
+    f->started = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    f->waiting = CreateEventW(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    active_fixture = f;
+    t_wait_reported = 0;
+    return f->started && f->waiting;
+}
+
+static void close_fixture(FIXTURE *f)
+{
+    CloseHandle(f->started);
+    CloseHandle(f->waiting);
+}
+
+static DWORD WINAPI waiter(LPVOID parameter)
+{
+    FIXTURE *f = parameter;
+    SetEvent(f->started);
+    xbox_nv2a_notify_wait(&f->wake, &f->get, &f->put,
+                         &f->notifications, 0, &f->stop);
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static int finish(HANDLE thread)
+{
+    if (WaitForSingleObject(thread, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "FAIL: guest wait did not complete\n");
+        /* Fixtures live on the calling stack; never return with a live user. */
+        ExitProcess(20);
+    }
+    CloseHandle(thread);
+    return !bad_timeout && !missed_wake;
+}
+
+static int completion_case(unsigned kind)
+{
+    FIXTURE f;
+    HANDLE thread;
+    if (!init_fixture(&f)) return 0;
+    if (kind == 4) { /* The host API is unavailable: retain yield fallback. */
+        f.wake.wait_address = NULL;
+        f.wake.wake_all = NULL;
+        if (!xbox_nv2a_wake_wait(&f.wake, 0)) return 0;
+    }
+    thread = CreateThread(NULL, 0, waiter, &f, 0, NULL);
+    if (!thread) return 0;
+    if (WaitForSingleObject(kind == 4 ? f.started : f.waiting, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0)
+        ExitProcess(21);
+    /* A host wake alone must not pretend that the GPU completed work. */
+    xbox_nv2a_wake_publish(&f.wake);
+    if (WaitForSingleObject(thread, 0) != WAIT_TIMEOUT) ExitProcess(22);
+    if (kind == 1) InterlockedIncrement(&f.notifications);
+    else if (kind == 2) InterlockedExchange(&f.stop, 1);
+    else f.get = f.put;
+    /* Guest-origin GET changes are found through the bounded timeout even
+     * when there is no corresponding executor notification. */
+    if (kind != 3) xbox_nv2a_wake_publish(&f.wake);
+    int okay = finish(thread);
+    close_fixture(&f);
+    return okay;
+}
+
+static int multiple_waiters(void)
+{
+    FIXTURE f;
+    HANDLE threads[4];
+    DWORD started = GetTickCount();
+    if (!init_fixture(&f)) return 0;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+        threads[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, waiter, &f, 0, NULL);
+        if (!threads[i]) ExitProcess(23);
+    }
+    while (InterlockedCompareExchange(&f.ready_count, 0, 0) != 4) {
+        if (GetTickCount() - started > 5000) ExitProcess(24);
+        Sleep(1);
+    }
+    f.get = f.put;
+    xbox_nv2a_wake_publish(&f.wake);
+    if (WaitForMultipleObjects(4, threads, TRUE, 5000) != WAIT_OBJECT_0) ExitProcess(25);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; i++) CloseHandle(threads[i]);
+    close_fixture(&f);
+    return !bad_timeout;
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+    FIXTURE f;
+    if (!init_fixture(&f)) return 10;
+    f.get = f.put; /* Completed before entering the helper: no host wait. */
+    xbox_nv2a_notify_wait(&f.wake, &f.get, &f.put, &f.notifications, 0, &f.stop);
+    if (f.wait_calls != 0) return 1;
+    close_fixture(&f);
+
+    if (!init_fixture(&f)) return 11;
+    f.inject_completion = 1;
+    xbox_nv2a_notify_wait(&f.wake, &f.get, &f.put, &f.notifications, 0, &f.stop);
+    if (f.wait_calls != 1 || missed_wake || bad_timeout) return 2;
+    close_fixture(&f);
+
+    for (unsigned kind = 0; kind < 5; kind++)
+        if (!completion_case(kind)) return 3 + kind;
+    if (!multiple_waiters()) return 8;
+    puts("PASS: early completion, check-to-wait race, GET/NOP/stop wakes, "
+         "spurious wake, bounded fallback and multiple guest waiters");
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_pb_hitch_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_pb_hitch_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..406c366
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/nv2a_pb_hitch_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,490 @@
+/* Use deterministic clocks and a synthetic command stream: tracing must not
+ * change decoding, callback order or guest command bytes. No GPU is started. */
+#include "kernel/kernel.h"
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+
+static int64_t test_wall, test_cpu;
+static unsigned clock_calls, kick_calls;
+static uint8_t *memory;
+static uint32_t mutate_payload_va;
+static struct { uint32_t subch, method, param; } commands[64];
+static unsigned command_count;
+static unsigned snapshot_calls;
+
+static BOOL WINAPI test_qpc(LARGE_INTEGER *value)
+{
+    clock_calls++;
+    value->QuadPart = test_wall;
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
+static BOOL WINAPI test_frequency(LARGE_INTEGER *value)
+{
+    value->QuadPart = 1000000;
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
+static BOOL WINAPI test_thread_times(HANDLE thread, LPFILETIME created,
+    LPFILETIME exited, LPFILETIME kernel, LPFILETIME user)
+{
+    (void)thread;
+    memset(created, 0, sizeof *created);
+    memset(exited, 0, sizeof *exited);
+    memset(kernel, 0, sizeof *kernel);
+    user->dwLowDateTime = (DWORD)test_cpu;
+    user->dwHighDateTime = (DWORD)(test_cpu >> 32);
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
+#define QueryPerformanceCounter test_qpc
+#define QueryPerformanceFrequency test_frequency
+#define GetThreadTimes test_thread_times
+#include "../../src/kernel/nv2a_pb_scan.c"
+#undef QueryPerformanceCounter
+#undef QueryPerformanceFrequency
+#undef GetThreadTimes
+
+ptrdiff_t xbox_GetMemoryOffset(void)
+{
+    return (ptrdiff_t)memory - (ptrdiff_t)XBOX_CONTIG_BASE;
+}
+
+void xbox_Nv2aCaptureSnapshot(XBOX_NV2A_CAPTURE_STATE *out)
+{
+    uint32_t low = XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x100000;
+    uint32_t high = low + 4u * 1024u * 1024u - 4u;
+    snapshot_calls++;
+    memset(out, 0, sizeof *out);
+    out->version = 1; out->bytes = sizeof *out; out->mirror_count = 1;
+    out->user_put = snapshot_calls; out->user_get = 7;
+    out->mirrors[0].device_bytes = XBOX_NV2A_CAPTURE_DEVICE_BYTES;
+    memcpy(out->mirrors[0].device + 0x24, &low, sizeof low);
+    memcpy(out->mirrors[0].device + 0x28, &high, sizeof high);
+}
+
+void nv2a_d3d_kick(void) { kick_calls++; }
+void nv2a_pb_exec_report(void) {}
+void nv2a_pb_exec_method(uint32_t subch, uint32_t method, uint32_t param)
+{
+    if (command_count >= 64) ExitProcess(30);
+    commands[command_count].subch = subch;
+    commands[command_count].method = method;
+    commands[command_count++].param = param;
+    if (mutate_payload_va && method == 0x1720 && param == 11) {
+        *(uint32_t *)(memory + mutate_payload_va) = 99;
+        mutate_payload_va = 0;
+        SetLastError(0x1357);
+    }
+    if (method == 0x17FC && !param) {
+        test_wall += 80000; /* A slow draw, independent of host scheduling. */
+        test_cpu += 400000; /* 40 ms of CPU within 80 ms of elapsed time. */
+    }
+    if (method == 0x0130) test_wall += 16000; /* Normal flip pacing. */
+}
+
+#define CHECK(condition) do { if (!(condition)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "FAIL line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #condition); return 1; \
+} } while (0)
+
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+    uint32_t *root, *called, *jumped;
+    uint32_t original[12];
+    int trace = argc > 1 && strcmp(argv[1], "trace") == 0;
+    int capture = argc > 1 && strcmp(argv[1], "capture") == 0;
+    CHECK(!capture || argc == 3);
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_PB_EXEC", "1");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_PB_SCAN", "");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_HITCH_TRACE", trace ? "1" : "0");
+    _putenv_s("RECOMP_PB_CAPTURE", capture ? argv[2] : "");
+    memory = calloc(1, XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE);
+    CHECK(memory);
+    root = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x100);
+    called = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x1000);
+    jumped = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x2000);
+    root[0] = (4u << 18) | (2u << 13) | 0x1720;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; i++) root[i + 1] = 10 + i;
+    root[5] = 0x40000000 | (4u << 18) | (3u << 13) | 0x1800;
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; i++) root[i + 6] = 20 + i;
+    root[10] = 0x1002; /* CALL */
+    root[11] = 0x2001; /* JUMP after RETURN */
+    called[0] = (1u << 18) | 0x17FC;
+    called[1] = 0;
+    called[2] = 0x00020000; /* RETURN */
+    /* FLIP_STALL at the end of an increasing packet must still count as
+     * pacing, rather than hide the slow draw in the non-flip maximum. */
+    jumped[0] = (5u << 18) | 0x0120;
+    for (unsigned i = 1; i <= 5; i++) jumped[i] = 0;
+    memcpy(original, root, sizeof original);
+    test_wall = 1000000;
+    nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x100, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x2018);
+    CHECK(kick_calls == 1 && command_count == 14);
+    CHECK(s_tot_calls == 1 && s_tot_jumps == 1 && !s_tot_unknown);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+        CHECK(commands[i].subch == 2 && commands[i].method == 0x1720 + i * 4);
+        CHECK(commands[i].param == 10 + i);
+        CHECK(commands[i + 4].subch == 3 && commands[i + 4].method == 0x1800);
+        CHECK(commands[i + 4].param == 20 + i);
+    }
+    CHECK(commands[8].method == 0x17FC && !commands[8].param);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < 5; i++)
+        CHECK(commands[9 + i].method == 0x0120 + i * 4 && !commands[9 + i].param);
+    CHECK(memcmp(original, root, sizeof original) == 0);
+    CHECK(trace ? clock_calls != 0 : clock_calls == 0);
+    CHECK(capture || snapshot_calls == 0);
+
+    /* PUT can stop after a header or in its payload. RETURN/CALL/JUMP-looking
+     * parameter values must remain data when the next submission arrives. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *split = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x400);
+        uint32_t saved[5];
+        command_count = 0;
+        split[0] = (4u << 18) | (2u << 13) | 0x1720;
+        split[1] = 0x00020000; split[2] = 0x1002;
+        split[3] = 0x2001; split[4] = 0x11223344;
+        memcpy(saved, split, sizeof saved);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x400, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x404);
+        CHECK(command_count == 0);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x404, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x408);
+        CHECK(command_count == 1 && commands[0].param == 0x00020000);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x408, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x410);
+        CHECK(command_count == 3);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x410, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x414);
+        CHECK(command_count == 4);
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+            CHECK(commands[i].subch == 2 && commands[i].method == 0x1720 + i * 4);
+            CHECK(commands[i].param == saved[i + 1]);
+        }
+        CHECK(memcmp(saved, split, sizeof saved) == 0);
+
+        command_count = 0;
+        split[0] = 0x40000000 | (3u << 18) | (3u << 13) | 0x1800;
+        split[1] = 0x2001; split[2] = 0x1002; split[3] = 0x00020000;
+        split[4] = (1u << 18) | 0x1D8C; split[5] = 32;
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x400, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x408);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x408, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x418);
+        CHECK(command_count == 4);
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
+            CHECK(commands[i].subch == 3 && commands[i].method == 0x1800);
+            CHECK(commands[i].param == split[i + 1]);
+        }
+        CHECK(commands[3].method == 0x1D8C && commands[3].param == 32);
+    }
+
+    /* Called lists reach RETURN even when their caller's PUT immediately
+     * follows CALL. The caller can then begin a split packet of its own. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *split = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x600);
+        command_count = 0;
+        split[0] = 0x1002;
+        split[1] = (3u << 18) | 0x1D8C;
+        split[2] = 1; split[3] = 2; split[4] = 3;
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x600, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x604);
+        CHECK(command_count == 1 && commands[0].method == 0x17FC);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x604, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x608);
+        CHECK(command_count == 1);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x608, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x614);
+        CHECK(command_count == 4);
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 3; i++)
+            CHECK(commands[i + 1].method == 0x1D8C + i * 4 && commands[i + 1].param == i + 1);
+    }
+
+    /* Complete a partial packet, follow an actual backwards ring JUMP,
+     * and suspend/resume the next packet in the low part of the ring. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *high = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x2F00);
+        uint32_t *low = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x800);
+        command_count = 0;
+        high[0] = (2u << 18) | 0x1720; high[1] = 0x11; high[2] = 0x22;
+        high[3] = 0x801;
+        low[0] = (2u << 18) | 0x1800; low[1] = 0x33; low[2] = 0x44;
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x2F00, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x2F08);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x2F08, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x804);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x804, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x80C);
+        CHECK(command_count == 4);
+        CHECK(commands[0].method == 0x1720 && commands[0].param == 0x11);
+        CHECK(commands[1].method == 0x1724 && commands[1].param == 0x22);
+        CHECK(commands[2].method == 0x1800 && commands[2].param == 0x33);
+        CHECK(commands[3].method == 0x1804 && commands[3].param == 0x44);
+    }
+
+    /* Sequential PFIFO reads and continuation aliases wrap on the26-bit bus. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *last = (uint32_t *)(memory + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE - 4);
+        uint32_t *first = (uint32_t *)memory;
+        command_count = 0;
+        *last = (2u << 18) | 0x1D8C; first[0] = 0x1002; first[1] = 0x2001;
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE - 4, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE);
+        CHECK(command_count == 0);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 8);
+        CHECK(command_count == 2);
+        CHECK(commands[0].method == 0x1D8C && commands[0].param == 0x1002);
+        CHECK(commands[1].method == 0x1D90 && commands[1].param == 0x2001);
+
+        /* A complete payload can cross the bus boundary within one scan. */
+        command_count = 0;
+        last[-1] = (3u << 18) | 0x1720; last[0] = 42;
+        first[0] = 0x1002; first[1] = 0x2001;
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE - 8, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 8);
+        CHECK(command_count == 3 && commands[0].param == 42);
+        CHECK(commands[1].method == 0x1724 && commands[1].param == 0x1002);
+        CHECK(commands[2].method == 0x1728 && commands[2].param == 0x2001);
+
+        /* Called lists use their RETURN, not the caller's PUT, and may wrap
+         * physical RAM before that RETURN without losing caller position. */
+        command_count = 0;
+        last[-1] = (1u << 18) | 0x17FC; last[0] = 0;
+        first[0] = 0x00020000;
+        root = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x900);
+        root[0] = (XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE - 8) | 2;
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x900, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x904);
+        CHECK(command_count == 1 && commands[0].method == 0x17FC);
+    }
+
+    /* An explicitly discontinuous scan cannot inherit stale packet state. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *old = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0xC00);
+        uint32_t *fresh = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0xD00);
+        command_count = 0;
+        old[0] = (3u << 18) | 0x1800;
+        fresh[0] = (1u << 18) | 0x1720; fresh[1] = 42;
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xC00, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xC04);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xD00, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xD08);
+        CHECK(command_count == 1 && commands[0].method == 0x1720 && commands[0].param == 42);
+    }
+
+    /* PUT bounds the actual FIFO even within a CALL. Its payload and saved
+     * return address survive publication; the caller then jumps around the
+     * list instead of decoding that list a second time. Address aliases are
+     * canonicalized before continuation matching. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *caller = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x5000);
+        uint32_t *list = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x5200);
+        uint32_t *tail = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x5300);
+        uint32_t saved[5];
+        command_count = 0;
+        caller[0] = 0x5202; caller[1] = 0x5301;
+        list[0] = (3u << 18) | 0x1720;
+        list[1] = 0x00020000; list[2] = 0x1002; list[3] = 0x2001;
+        list[4] = 0x00020000;
+        tail[0] = (1u << 18) | 0x1D8C; tail[1] = 77;
+        memcpy(saved, list, sizeof saved);
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x5000, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x5208));
+        CHECK(command_count == 1 && commands[0].param == 0x00020000);
+        CHECK(s_fifo.in_call && s_packet.active && s_packet.remaining == 2);
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE + 0x5208,
+                           XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE + 0x5308));
+        CHECK(command_count == 4 && !s_fifo.in_call && !s_packet.active);
+        for (unsigned i = 0; i < 3; ++i)
+            CHECK(commands[i].method == 0x1720 + i * 4 && commands[i].param == saved[i + 1]);
+        CHECK(commands[3].method == 0x1D8C && commands[3].param == 77);
+        CHECK(!memcmp(saved, list, sizeof saved));
+
+        /* A CALL can land directly on PUT, before any header is published. */
+        command_count = 0;
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x5000, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x5200));
+        CHECK(command_count == 0 && s_fifo.in_call && !s_packet.active);
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x5200, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x5308));
+        CHECK(command_count == 4 && !s_fifo.in_call);
+    }
+
+    /* The PUT comparison also wraps correctly in a called payload. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *last = (uint32_t *)(memory + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE - 4);
+        uint32_t *first = (uint32_t *)memory;
+        uint32_t *caller = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x9000);
+        uint32_t *tail = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x9400);
+        command_count = 0;
+        caller[0] = (XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE - 8) | 2; caller[1] = 0x9401;
+        last[-1] = (3u << 18) | 0x1720; last[0] = 11;
+        first[0] = 22; first[1] = 33; first[2] = 0x00020000;
+        tail[0] = (1u << 18) | 0x1D8C; tail[1] = 44;
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x9000, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 4));
+        CHECK(command_count == 2 && s_fifo.in_call && s_packet.remaining == 1);
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 4, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x9408));
+        CHECK(command_count == 4 && !s_fifo.in_call && !s_packet.active);
+        CHECK(commands[0].param == 11 && commands[1].param == 22);
+        CHECK(commands[2].method == 0x1728 && commands[2].param == 33);
+        CHECK(commands[3].method == 0x1D8C && commands[3].param == 44);
+    }
+
+    /* RETURN is the exact00020000 word; reserved high bits cannot create a
+     * fake method packet and consume the next valid header as a parameter. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *caller = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0xA000);
+        uint32_t *list = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0xB000);
+        uint32_t before_unknown = s_tot_unknown;
+        command_count = 0;
+        caller[0] = 0xB002;
+        list[0] = 0x00020004;
+        list[1] = 0x60000000 | (1u << 18) | 0x1720;
+        list[2] = (1u << 18) | 0x1D8C; list[3] = 55;
+        list[4] = 0x00020000;
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xA000, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xA004));
+        CHECK(command_count == 1 && commands[0].method == 0x1D8C && commands[0].param == 55);
+        CHECK(s_tot_unknown - before_unknown == 2 && !s_fifo.in_call);
+    }
+
+    /* Increasing method addresses retain the register's11-bit field width,
+     * including a payload split at the wrap. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *split = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0xC100);
+        command_count = 0;
+        split[0] = (3u << 18) | 0x1FFC; split[1] = 10;
+        split[2] = 20; split[3] = 30;
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xC100, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xC108));
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xC108, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xC110));
+        CHECK(command_count == 3);
+        CHECK(commands[0].method == 0x1FFC && commands[0].param == 10);
+        CHECK(commands[1].method == 0 && commands[1].param == 20);
+        CHECK(commands[2].method == 4 && commands[2].param == 30);
+    }
+
+    /* A scheduling cap is incomplete, including inside a payload. Retrying
+     * the original start with a newer PUT executes the saved remainder once
+     * and does not skip the additional publication. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *stream = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x100000);
+        uint32_t start = XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x100000;
+        uint32_t old_end = start + (0x100000u + 2) * 4;
+        uint32_t before_words = s_tot_words;
+        command_count = 0;
+        memset(stream, 0, (0x100000u + 4) * 4);
+        stream[0x100000u - 2] = (3u << 18) | 0x1720;
+        stream[0x100000u - 1] = 11;
+        stream[0x100000u] = 22; stream[0x100000u + 1] = 33;
+        stream[0x100000u + 2] = (1u << 18) | 0x1D8C;
+        stream[0x100000u + 3] = 44;
+        if (capture) mutate_payload_va = 0x100000 + (0x100000u - 1) * 4;
+        CHECK(!nv2a_pb_scan(start, old_end));
+        CHECK(s_tot_words - before_words == 0x100000u);
+        CHECK(command_count == 1 && s_packet.active && s_packet.remaining == 2);
+        if (capture) {
+            const char *suffixes[] = { ".ram.bin", ".reads.bin", ".recent.bin", ".json",
+                ".initial-ring.bin", ".state-initial.bin", ".state-final.bin", ".producer.json" };
+            char path[4096], metadata[4096];
+            PB_CAPTURE_READ recorded;
+            XBOX_NV2A_CAPTURE_STATE state;
+            uint32_t copied;
+            FILE *file;
+            CHECK(GetLastError() == 0x1357);
+            CHECK(s_capture.done && !s_capture.first && !s_capture.ring && !s_capture.recording);
+            snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s.reads.bin", argv[2]);
+            file = fopen(path, "rb"); CHECK(file);
+            CHECK(!fseek(file, 0, SEEK_END));
+            CHECK(ftell(file) == (long)(0x100000u * sizeof recorded));
+            CHECK(!fseek(file, -(long)sizeof recorded, SEEK_END));
+            CHECK(fread(&recorded, sizeof recorded, 1, file) == 1);
+            CHECK(!fclose(file));
+            snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s.initial-ring.bin", argv[2]);
+            file = fopen(path, "rb"); CHECK(file);
+            CHECK(!fseek(file, 0, SEEK_END) && ftell(file) == 4u * 1024u * 1024u);
+            CHECK(!fseek(file, -(long)sizeof copied, SEEK_END));
+            CHECK(fread(&copied, sizeof copied, 1, file) == 1 && copied == 11);
+            CHECK(!fclose(file));
+            snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s.state-initial.bin", argv[2]);
+            file = fopen(path, "rb"); CHECK(file);
+            CHECK(fread(&state, sizeof state, 1, file) == 1);
+            CHECK(!fclose(file) && state.user_put + 1 == snapshot_calls);
+            snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s.state-final.bin", argv[2]);
+            file = fopen(path, "rb"); CHECK(file);
+            CHECK(fread(&state, sizeof state, 1, file) == 1);
+            CHECK(!fclose(file) && state.user_put == snapshot_calls);
+            CHECK(recorded.va == start + (0x100000u - 1) * 4);
+            CHECK(recorded.word == 11 && recorded.method == 0x1720);
+            CHECK(recorded.remaining == 3 && recorded.flags == 1);
+            snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s.ram.bin", argv[2]);
+            file = fopen(path, "rb"); CHECK(file);
+            CHECK(!fseek(file, 0, SEEK_END) && ftell(file) == XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE);
+            CHECK(!fseek(file, (long)(recorded.va - XBOX_CONTIG_BASE), SEEK_SET));
+            CHECK(fread(&copied, sizeof copied, 1, file) == 1 && copied == 99);
+            CHECK(!fclose(file));
+            snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s.recent.bin", argv[2]);
+            file = fopen(path, "rb"); CHECK(file);
+            CHECK(!fseek(file, -(long)sizeof recorded, SEEK_END));
+            CHECK(fread(&recorded, sizeof recorded, 1, file) == 1 && recorded.word == 11);
+            CHECK(!fclose(file));
+            snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s.json", argv[2]);
+            file = fopen(path, "rb"); CHECK(file);
+            size_t length = fread(metadata, 1, sizeof metadata - 1, file);
+            metadata[length] = 0; CHECK(!fclose(file));
+            CHECK(strstr(metadata, "\"first_reads\":1048576"));
+            CHECK(strstr(metadata, "\"ram_ok\":1,\"first_ok\":1,\"recent_ok\":1"));
+            CHECK(strstr(metadata, "\"initial_ring_bytes\":4194304,\"initial_ring_ok\":1"));
+            CHECK(strstr(metadata, "\"initial_state_ok\":1,\"final_state_ok\":1,\"producer_ok\":1"));
+            snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s.producer.json", argv[2]);
+            file = fopen(path, "rb"); CHECK(file);
+            length = fread(metadata, 1, sizeof metadata - 1, file);
+            metadata[length] = 0; CHECK(!fclose(file));
+            CHECK(strstr(metadata, "\"initial\":{\"version\":1"));
+            CHECK(strstr(metadata, "\"final\":{\"version\":1"));
+            CHECK(strstr(metadata, "\"ring_high\":2152726524"));
+            for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof suffixes / sizeof suffixes[0]; i++) {
+                snprintf(path, sizeof path, "%s%s", argv[2], suffixes[i]);
+                CHECK(!remove(path));
+            }
+        }
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(start + XBOX_CONTIG_SIZE, old_end + 8));
+        CHECK(command_count == 4 && !s_packet.active && !s_fifo.active);
+        CHECK(commands[0].method == 0x1720 && commands[0].param == 11);
+        CHECK(commands[1].method == 0x1724 && commands[1].param == 22);
+        CHECK(commands[2].method == 0x1728 && commands[2].param == 33);
+        CHECK(commands[3].method == 0x1D8C && commands[3].param == 44);
+    }
+
+    /* Called lists share the root's cap; they neither enlarge it nor lose the
+     * saved return PC when the next ACK tick resumes their header. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *caller = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0xC5000);
+        uint32_t *list = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0x800000);
+        uint32_t start = XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xC5000;
+        uint32_t before_words = s_tot_words;
+        command_count = 0;
+        memset(list, 0, (0x100000u + 2) * 4);
+        caller[0] = 0x800002; caller[1] = 0xC5011;
+        caller[4] = (1u << 18) | 0x1D8C; caller[5] = 66;
+        list[0x100000u - 1] = (1u << 18) | 0x1720;
+        list[0x100000u] = 55; list[0x100000u + 1] = 0x00020000;
+        CHECK(!nv2a_pb_scan(start, start + 24));
+        CHECK(s_tot_words - before_words == 0x100000u);
+        CHECK(command_count == 0 && s_fifo.in_call);
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(start, start + 24));
+        CHECK(command_count == 2 && !s_fifo.active && !s_fifo.in_call);
+        CHECK(commands[0].method == 0x1720 && commands[0].param == 55);
+        CHECK(commands[1].method == 0x1D8C && commands[1].param == 66);
+    }
+
+    /* A discontinuous replacement discards an unfinished called list as well
+     * as its packet; it cannot return into a previous FIFO. */
+    {
+        uint32_t *caller = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0xE000);
+        uint32_t *list = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0xE200);
+        uint32_t *fresh = (uint32_t *)(memory + 0xE400);
+        command_count = 0;
+        caller[0] = 0xE202;
+        list[0] = (3u << 18) | 0x1720; list[1] = 12;
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xE000, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xE208));
+        CHECK(command_count == 1 && s_fifo.in_call && s_packet.active);
+        fresh[0] = (1u << 18) | 0x1D8C; fresh[1] = 34;
+        CHECK(nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xE400, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0xE408));
+        CHECK(command_count == 2 && commands[1].method == 0x1D8C && commands[1].param == 34);
+        CHECK(!s_fifo.in_call && !s_packet.active);
+    }
+
+    /* Empty packets execute nothing and need no per-packet diagnostic clock. */
+    {
+        unsigned before_clocks = clock_calls;
+        command_count = 0;
+        memset(memory + 0x1800, 0, 1000 * 4);
+        nv2a_pb_scan(XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x1800, XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x27A0);
+        CHECK(command_count == 0);
+        CHECK(clock_calls - before_clocks == (trace ? 2u : 0u));
+    }
+    CHECK(trace ? clock_calls != 0 : clock_calls == 0);
+    CHECK(capture ? snapshot_calls > 1 : snapshot_calls == 0);
+    free(memory);
+    puts("PASS: tracing, PUT/cap continuations, exact decoding and ring/bus wraps preserve command order");
+    return 0;
+}
diff --git a/tests/kernel_dispatch/reserve_heap_ownership_test.c b/tests/kernel_dispatch/reserve_heap_ownership_test.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d0a5541
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/kernel_dispatch/reserve_heap_ownership_test.c
@@ -0,0 +1,170 @@
+/* Production allocator regression: above-RAM reservations and the mapped
+ * ordinary heap must never grant the same bytes, in either allocation order. */
+#include "kernel.h"
+#include "xbox_memory_layout.h"
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+#include "../../src/kernel/xbox_memory_layout.c"
+
+void *recomp_lookup(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+void *recomp_lookup_manual(ULONG address) { (void)address; abort(); }
+
+#define CHECK(expr) do { if (!(expr)) { \
+    fprintf(stderr, "line %d: %s\n", __LINE__, #expr); exit(1); \
+} } while (0)
+#define RAM_END 0x04000000u
+#define MAP_END 0x08000000u
+
+static uint8_t *bytes(uint32_t address)
+{
+    return (uint8_t *)((uintptr_t)address + g_memory_offset);
+}
+
+static void expect_bytes(uint32_t address, uint32_t size, uint8_t value)
+{
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < size; ++i) CHECK(bytes(address)[i] == value);
+}
+
+static void reset_allocators(void)
+{
+    g_heap_next = XBOX_HEAP_BASE;
+    g_heap_block_count = 0;
+    g_heap_alloc_count = 0;
+    g_reserve_next = 0;
+    g_reserve_alloc_count = 0;
+    t_reserve_begin = t_reserve_end = 0;
+    g_contig_alloc_count = 0;
+    g_contig_next = XBOX_CONTIG_BASE + 0x1000;
+}
+
+static void check_ownership(void)
+{
+    for (int i = 0; i < g_reserve_alloc_count; ++i) {
+        uint64_t begin = g_reserve_allocs[i].addr;
+        uint64_t end = begin + g_reserve_allocs[i].size;
+        CHECK(begin >= RAM_END && end <= MAP_END);
+        if (i) CHECK((uint64_t)g_reserve_allocs[i - 1].addr +
+                     g_reserve_allocs[i - 1].size <= begin);
+        for (int j = 0; j < g_heap_block_count; ++j)
+            CHECK(end <= g_heap_blocks[j].addr ||
+                  (uint64_t)g_heap_blocks[j].addr + g_heap_blocks[j].size <= begin);
+    }
+}
+
+enum { THREADS = 8, ALLOCS_PER_THREAD = 128 };
+static HANDLE start_event;
+static DWORD WINAPI allocation_worker(void *context)
+{
+    uintptr_t kind = (uintptr_t)context;
+    CHECK(WaitForSingleObject(start_event, 10000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < ALLOCS_PER_THREAD; ++i) {
+        uint32_t address = kind & 1
+            ? xbox_ReserveAlloc(4096, 4096) : xbox_HeapAlloc(4096, 4096);
+        CHECK(address);
+        memset(bytes(address), (int)(kind + 1), 4096);
+    }
+    return 0;
+}
+
+int main(void)
+{
+    uint8_t *arena = VirtualAlloc(NULL, MAP_END, MEM_RESERVE | MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+    uint32_t reservation, heap, second, next;
+    HANDLE workers[THREADS];
+    CHECK(arena);
+    g_memory_offset = (ptrdiff_t)arena;
+    g_memory_size = MAP_END;
+    g_xbox_map_size = MAP_END;
+    g_xbox_total_ram = RAM_END;
+    InitializeCriticalSection(&g_allocator_lock);
+    g_allocator_lock_initialized = 1;
+    SetEnvironmentVariableA("RECOMP_HEAP_WATCH", NULL);
+
+    /* This is the menu-stall layout: CRT reserves at 64 MB before the
+     * ordinary heap grows across that address. No allocator may zero it. */
+    reservation = xbox_ReserveAlloc(0x100000, 4096);
+    CHECK(reservation == RAM_END);
+    memset(bytes(reservation), 0xA5, 0x100000);
+    g_heap_next = RAM_END - 4096;
+    heap = xbox_HeapAlloc(8192, 4096);
+    CHECK(heap == RAM_END + 0x100000);
+    expect_bytes(reservation, 0x100000, 0xA5);
+    check_ownership();
+
+    /* A reservation made later must skip live and freed heap blocks. */
+    reset_allocators();
+    g_heap_next = RAM_END;
+    heap = xbox_HeapAlloc(8192, 4096);
+    memset(bytes(heap), 0x3C, 8192);
+    xbox_HeapFree(heap);
+    reservation = xbox_ReserveAlloc(0x100000, 4096);
+    CHECK(reservation == RAM_END + 8192);
+    CHECK(!xbox_ReserveRangeAllocated(heap));
+    memset(bytes(reservation), 0xA5, 0x100000);
+    expect_bytes(heap, 8192, 0x3C);
+    CHECK(xbox_HeapAlloc(8192, 4096) == heap);
+    expect_bytes(reservation, 0x100000, 0xA5);
+    check_ownership();
+
+    /* Alignment and skipped heap bytes do not become reservation coverage. */
+    reset_allocators();
+    g_heap_next = RAM_END + 0x10000;
+    heap = xbox_HeapAlloc(8192, 4096);
+    reservation = xbox_ReserveAlloc(8192, 4096);
+    second = xbox_ReserveAlloc(8192, 0x10000);
+    CHECK(reservation == RAM_END && second == RAM_END + 0x20000);
+    CHECK(xbox_ReserveRangeAllocated(reservation + 8191));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ReserveRangeAllocated(reservation + 8192));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ReserveRangeAllocated(heap));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ReserveRangeAllocated(second - 1));
+    CHECK(xbox_ReserveRangeAllocated(second));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ReserveRangeAllocated(second + 8192));
+    next = xbox_HeapAlloc(8192, 4096);
+    CHECK(next == RAM_END + 0x12000);
+    check_ownership();
+
+    /* All failing arithmetic leaves ownership/high-water metadata intact. */
+    next = g_reserve_next;
+    CHECK(!xbox_ReserveAlloc(0xFFFFFFFFu, 4096));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ReserveAlloc(4096, 0x80000000u));
+    CHECK(!xbox_ReserveAlloc(4096, 12288));
+    CHECK(g_reserve_next == next);
+    next = g_heap_next;
+    CHECK(!xbox_HeapAlloc(0xFFFFFFFFu, 4096));
+    CHECK(!xbox_HeapAlloc(4096, 0x80000000u));
+    CHECK(!xbox_HeapAlloc(4096, 12288));
+    CHECK(g_heap_next == next);
+    check_ownership();
+
+    /* Simultaneous reservations cannot race each other or heap allocation. */
+    reset_allocators();
+    g_heap_next = RAM_END;
+    start_event = CreateEventA(NULL, TRUE, FALSE, NULL);
+    CHECK(start_event);
+    for (uintptr_t i = 0; i < THREADS; ++i) {
+        workers[i] = CreateThread(NULL, 0, allocation_worker, (void *)i, 0, NULL);
+        CHECK(workers[i]);
+    }
+    CHECK(SetEvent(start_event));
+    CHECK(WaitForMultipleObjects(THREADS, workers, TRUE, 10000) == WAIT_OBJECT_0);
+    for (unsigned i = 0; i < THREADS; ++i) {
+        DWORD code;
+        CHECK(GetExitCodeThread(workers[i], &code) && code == 0);
+        CloseHandle(workers[i]);
+    }
+    CloseHandle(start_event);
+    CHECK(g_reserve_alloc_count == THREADS / 2 * ALLOCS_PER_THREAD);
+    CHECK(g_heap_block_count == THREADS / 2 * ALLOCS_PER_THREAD);
+    check_ownership();
+
+    /* A retail-sized mapping still has no above-RAM reserve arena. */
+    g_memory_size = RAM_END;
+    CHECK(!xbox_ReserveAlloc(4096, 4096));
+    DeleteCriticalSection(&g_allocator_lock);
+    CHECK(VirtualFree(arena, 0, MEM_RELEASE));
+    puts("reserve/heap exact ownership, arithmetic and concurrency passed");
+    return 0;
+}
